iao:0000100 iao:0000111 "data set"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Intensity values in a CEL file or from multiple CEL files comprise a data set (as opposed to the CEL files themselves)."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A data item that is an aggregate of other data items of the same type that have something in common. Averages and distributions can be determined for data sets."@en;
            iao:0000116 "2009/10/23 Alan Ruttenberg. The intention is that this term represent collections of like data. So this isn't for, e.g. the whole contents of a cel file, which includes parameters, metadata etc. This is more like java arrays of a certain rather specific type"@en,
                        "2014-05-05: Data sets are aggregates and thus must include two or more data items. We have chosen not to add logical axioms to make this restriction.";
