                                                                         owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000059 ; 
                                                                         a owl:Restriction] ; 
                                                     owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000053 ; 
                                                     a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                 a owl:Class].
iao:0000219 iao:0000112 """A person's name denotes the person. A variable name in a computer program denotes some piece of memory. Lexically equivalent strings can denote different things, for instance \"Alan\" can denote different people. In each case of use, there is a case of the denotation relation obtaining, between \"Alan\" and the person that is being named."""@en;
            iao:0000115 "denotes is a primitive, instance-level, relation obtaining between an information content entity and some portion of reality. Denotation is what happens when someone creates an information content entity E in order to specifically refer to something. The only relation between E and the thing is that E can be used to 'pick out' the thing. This relation connects those two together. Freedictionary.com sense 3: To signify directly; refer to specifically"@en;
            iao:0000116 """2009-11-10 Alan Ruttenberg. Old definition said the following to emphasize the generic nature of this relation. We no longer have 'specifically denotes', which would have been primitive, so make this relation primitive.
g denotes r =def 
r is a portion of reality
there is some c that is a concretization of g 
every c that is a concretization of g specifically denotes r"""@en;
            iao:0000117 "person:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            iao:0000119 "Conversations with Barry Smith, Werner Ceusters, Bjoern Peters, Michel Dumontier, Melanie Courtot, James Malone, Bill Hogan"@en;
            a owl:ObjectProperty;
            rdfs:comment ""@en;
            rdfs:label "denotes"@en;
            rdfs:subPropertyOf iao:0000136.
iao:0000220 iao:0000116 "see https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/25&q=denote";
            iao:0000231 iao:0000103;
            a owl:ObjectProperty;
            rdfs:label "obsolete_materially denotes";
            rdfs:subPropertyOf oboinowl:ObsoleteProperty;
            owl:deprecated true.
iao:0000221 iao:0000115 """m is a quality measurement of q at t when
q is a quality 
there is a measurement process p that has specified output m, a measurement datum, that is about q"""@en;
            iao:0000116 """This one is the one we are struggling with at the moment. The issue is what a measurement measures. On the one hand saying that it measures the quality would include it \"measuring\" the bearer = referring to the bearer in the measurement. However this makes comparisons of two different things not possible. On the other hand not having it inhere in the bearer, on the face of it, breaks the audit trail.

Werner suggests a solution based on \"Magnitudes\" a proposal for which we are awaiting details."""@en,
                        """From the second IAO workshop [Alan Ruttenberg 8/6/2009: not completely current, though bringing in comparison is probably important]

This one is the one we are struggling with at the moment. The issue is what a measurement measures. On the one hand saying that it measures the quality would include it \"measuring\" the bearer = referring to the bearer in the measurement. However this makes comparisons of two different things not possible. On the other hand not having it inhere in the bearer, on the face of it, breaks the audit trail.

Werner suggests a solution based on \"Magnitudes\" a proposal for which we are awaiting details.
--
From the second IAO workshop, various comments, [commented on by Alan Ruttenberg 8/6/2009]

unit of measure is a quality, e.g. the length of a ruler.

[We decided to hedge on what units of measure are, instead talking about measurement unit labels, which are the information content entities that are about whatever measurement units are. For IAO we need that information entity in any case. See the term measurement unit label]

[Some struggling with the various subflavors of is_about. We subsequently removed the relation represents, and describes until and only when we have a better theory]

a represents b means either a denotes b or a describes

describe:
a describes b means a is about b and a allows an inference of at least one quality of b

We have had a long discussion about denotes versus describes."""@en,
                        """From the second meeting on IAO:

An attempt at defining assay using Barry's \"reliability\" wording

assay:
process and has_input some material entity
and has_output some information content entity 
and which is such that instances of this process type reliably generate 
outputs that describes the input."""@en,
                        """From the second IAO workshop: An attempt at tieing the quality to the measurement datum more carefully.

a is a magnitude means a is a determinate quality particular inhering in some bearer b existing at a time t that can be represented/denoted by an information content entity e that has parts denoting a unit of measure, a number, and b. The unit of measure is an instance of the determinable quality."""@en,
                        "8/6/2009 Alan Ruttenberg: The strategy is to be rather specific with this relationship. There are other kinds of measurements that are not of qualities, such as those that measure time. We will add these as separate properties for the moment and see about generalizing later"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            a owl:ObjectProperty;
            rdfs:domain iao:0000109;
            rdfs:label "is quality measurement of"@en;
            rdfs:range pobo:BFO_0000019;
            rdfs:subPropertyOf iao:0000136;
            owl:equivalentProperty [owl:inverseOf iao:0000417];
            owl:inverseOf iao:0000417.
iao:0000222 iao:0000231 iao:0000103;
            a owl:ObjectProperty;
            rdfs:label "obsolete_describes";
            rdfs:subPropertyOf oboinowl:ObsoleteProperty;
            owl:deprecated true.
iao:0000223 iao:0000231 iao:0000103;
            a owl:ObjectProperty;
            rdfs:label "obsolete_represents";
            rdfs:subPropertyOf oboinowl:ObsoleteProperty;
            owl:deprecated true.
iao:0000224 iao:0000115 "Core is an instance of a grouping of terms from an ontology or ontologies. It is used by the ontology to identify main classes."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            a oboinowl:Subset,
              owl:NamedIndividual;
            rdfs:label "core"@en.
iao:0000225 iao:0000111 "obsolescence reason specification"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "The reason for which a term has been deprecated. The allowed values come from an enumerated list of predefined terms. See the specification of these instances for more detailed definitions of each enumerated value."@en;
            iao:0000116 "The creation of this class has been inspired in part by Werner Ceusters' paper, Applying evolutionary terminology auditing to the Gene Ontology."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en,
                        "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "obsolescence reason specification"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000102;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:oneOf (iao:0000103
                                            iao:0000226
                                            iao:0000227
                                            iao:0000228
                                            iao:0000229) ; 
                                 a owl:Class].
iao:0000226 a iao:0000225,
              owl:NamedIndividual,
              owl:Thing;
            rdfs:label "placeholder removed"@en.
iao:0000227 iao:0000116 "An editor note should explain what were the merged terms and the reason for the merge."@en;
            a iao:0000225,
              owl:NamedIndividual;
            rdfs:label "terms merged"@en.
iao:0000228 iao:0000116 "This is to be used when the original term has been replaced by a term imported from an other ontology. An editor note should indicate what is the URI of the new term to use."@en;
            a iao:0000225,
              owl:NamedIndividual;
            rdfs:label "term imported"@en.
iao:0000229 iao:0000116 "This is to be used when a term has been split in two or more new terms. An editor note should indicate the reason for the split and indicate the URIs of the new terms created."@en;
            a iao:0000225,
              owl:NamedIndividual;
            rdfs:label "term split"@en.
iao:0000230 iao:0000116 "We expect to be able to mine these new reasons and add instances as required."@en,
                        "This is to be used if none of the existing instances cover the reason for obsolescence. An editor note should indicate this new reason."@en;
            a iao:0000225,
              owl:NamedIndividual;
            rdfs:label "other"@en;
            owl:deprecated true.
iao:0000231 iao:0000111 "has obsolescence reason"@en;
            iao:0000115 "Relates an annotation property to an obsolescence reason. The values of obsolescence reasons come from a list of predefined terms, instances of the class obsolescence reason specification."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "PERSON:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            a owl:AnnotationProperty;
            rdfs:label "has obsolescence reason"@en.
iao:0000232 iao:0000111 "curator note"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An administrative note of use for a curator but of no use for a user"@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            a owl:AnnotationProperty;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy pobo:iao.owl;
            rdfs:label "curator note"@en.
iao:0000233 iao:0000111 "term tracker item";
            iao:0000112 "the URI for an OBI Terms ticket at sourceforge, such as https://sourceforge.net/p/obi/obi-terms/772/";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "An IRI or similar locator for a request or discussion of an ontology term.";
            iao:0000117 "Person: Jie Zheng, Chris Stoeckert, Alan Ruttenberg";
