"""@en;
            iao:0000115 "A macro expansion tag applied to an object property (or possibly a data property)  which can be used by a macro-expansion engine to generate more complex expressions from simpler ones"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Chris Mungall";
            a owl:AnnotationProperty;
            rdfs:label "expand expression to"@en.
iao:0000425 iao:0000111 "expand assertion to"@en;
            iao:0000112 """ObjectProperty: RO???
Label: spatially disjoint from
Annotations: expand_assertion_to \"DisjointClasses: (http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051 some ?X)  (http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051 some ?Y)\"
"""@en;
            iao:0000115 "A macro expansion tag applied to an annotation property which can be expanded into a more detailed axiom."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Chris Mungall"@en;
            a owl:AnnotationProperty;
            rdfs:label "expand assertion to"@en.
iao:0000426 iao:0000111 "first order logic expression"@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            a owl:AnnotationProperty;
            rdfs:label "first order logic expression"@en.
iao:0000427 iao:0000111 "antisymmetric property"@en;
            iao:0000112 "part_of antisymmetric property xsd:true"@en;
            iao:0000115 "use boolean value xsd:true to indicate that the property is an antisymmetric property"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            a owl:AnnotationProperty;
            rdfs:label "antisymmetric property"@en.
iao:0000428 iao:0000115 "A term that is metadata complete, has been reviewed, and problems have been identified that require discussion before release. Such a term requires editor note(s) to identify the outstanding issues."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            iao:0000119 "group:OBI"@en;
            a iao:0000078,
              owl:NamedIndividual;
            rdfs:label "requires discussion"@en.
iao:0000429 iao:0000111 "email address"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000116 "Alan Ruttenberg 1/3/2012 - Provisional id, see issue at https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/130&thanks=130&ts=1325636583"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Person:Chris Stoeckart"@en,
                        "Person:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "email address"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030.
iao:0000442 iao:0000111 "author role"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A role inhering in a person or organization that is realized when the bearer participates in the work which is the basis of the document, in the writing of the document, and signs it with their name."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "author role"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000023.
iao:0000443 iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "a planned process in which journal articles are read or processed and data items are extracted, typically for further analysis or indexing";
            iao:0000117 "Person:Alan Ruttenberg";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "data item extraction from journal article";
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000027 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000013 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000011.
iao:0000572 iao:0000112 "Recording the current temperature in a laboratory notebook. Writing a journal article. Updating a patient record in a database."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "a planned process in which a document is created or added to by including the specified input in it."@en;
            iao:0000116 "6/11/9: Edited at OBI workshop. We need to be able identify a child form of information artifact which corresponds to something enduring (not brain like). This used to be restricted to physical document or digital entity as the output, but that excludes e.g. an audio cassette tape"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Bjoern Peters"@en;
            iao:0000119 "wikipedia http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Documenting"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "documenting"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000011,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000310 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000030 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
iao:0000573 iao:0000111 "line graph"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 """A line graph is a type of graph created by connecting a series of data
points together with a line."""@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Chris Stoeckert"@en,
                        "PERSON:Melanie Courtot"@en;
            iao:0000118 "line chart"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Line_chart"@en,
                        "GROUP:OBI"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "line graph"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000038.
iao:0000574 iao:0000112 "A new pubmed ID being created for a journal article, and the associated pubmed record containing information to the journal article. A license plate number registered at the DMV to be belonging to a specific vehicle and owner. Placing a barcode on a product and entering information in a database that this barcode is assigned."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "a planned process in which a new CRID is created, associated with an entity, and stored in the CRID registry thereby registering it as being associated with some entity"@en;
            iao:0000116 "2014-05-05: It is the CRID registry that assigns CRIDs, not the users of the registry."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Person:Alan Ruttenberg"@en,
                        "Person:Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "Person:Bjoern Peters"@en;
            iao:0000118 "assigning a CRID";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "assigning a centrally registered identifier"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000577 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000011,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000579 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000057 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
iao:0000575 iao:0000112 "Articles in Pubmed are reviewed by curators who add MESH terms to the Pubmed records in order to categorize them better and improve the ability to search for them. ";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A planned process in which a CRID registry associates an information content entity with a CRID symbol"@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            iao:0000118 "associating information with a CRID in the CRID registry";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "associating information with a centrally registered identifier in its registry"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000577 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000011,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000579 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000057 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000030 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
iao:0000576 iao:0000115 "a planned process with the objective to establish a system that allows to refer to specific entities of a certain kind and store information about them, by establishing a CRID registry and plan specifications for the process of 1) assigning a CRID and 2) looking up a CRID.";
            iao:0000116 "MC, 20101124: deprecated following discussion at IAO call 20101124. Term was deemed not necessary - no use case for now.";
            iao:0000231 iao:0000103;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "obsolete_establishing a CRID registry";
            rdfs:subClassOf oboinowl:ObsoleteClass;
            owl:deprecated true.
iao:0000577 iao:0000112 """The sentence \"The article has Pubmed ID 12345.\" contains a CRID that has two parts: one part is the CRID symbol, which is '12345'; the other part denotes the CRID registry, which is Pubmed."""@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A symbol that is part of a CRID and that is sufficient to look up a record from the CRID's registry."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Bill Hogan"@en,
                        "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en,
                        "PERSON: Bjoern Peters"@en,
                        "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en;
            iao:0000118 "CRID symbol";
            iao:0000119 "Original proposal from Bjoern, discussions at IAO calls"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "centrally registered identifier symbol"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000578 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000050 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            iao:0000028.
iao:0000578 iao:0000112 """The sentence \"The article has Pubmed ID 12345.\" contains a CRID that has two parts: one part is the CRID symbol, which is '12345'; the other part denotes the CRID registry, which is Pubmed."""@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An information content entity that consists of a CRID symbol and additional information about the CRID registry to which it belongs."@en;
            iao:0000116 "2014-05-05: In defining this term we take no position on what the CRID denotes. In particular do not assume it denotes a *record* in the CRID registry (since the registry might not have 'records')."@en,
                        """Alan, IAO call 20101124: potentially the CRID denotes the instance it was associated with during creation. 
"""@en,
                        "Note, IAO call 20101124: URIs are not always CRID, as not centrally registered. We acknowledge that CRID is a subset of a larger identifier class, but this subset fulfills our current needs. OBI PURLs are CRID as they are registered with OCLC. UPCs (Universal Product Codes from AC Nielsen)are not CRID as they are not centrally registered."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "PERSON: Bjoern Peters"@en,
                        "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en,
                        "PERSON: Bill Hogan"@en;
            iao:0000118 "CRID";
            iao:0000119 "Original proposal from Bjoern, discussions at IAO calls"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "centrally registered identifier"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000579 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty iao:0000219 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction] ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000051 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            iao:0000030,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000577 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000051 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
iao:0000579 iao:0000112 "PubMed is a CRID registry. It has a dataset of PubMed identifiers associated with journal articles. "@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A CRID registry is a dataset of CRID records, each consisting of a CRID symbol and additional information which was recorded in the dataset through a assigning a centrally registered identifier process."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Bill Hogan"@en,
                        "PERSON: Bjoern Peters"@en,
                        "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en,
                        "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en;
            iao:0000118 "CRID registry";
            iao:0000119 "Original proposal from Bjoern, discussions at IAO calls"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "centrally registered identifier registry"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000100.
iao:0000580 iao:0000112 "Going to the PubMed website and entering a PubMed ID in order to retrieve the Pubmed information associated with that ID. ";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A planned process in which a request to a CRID registry is made to return the information associated with a CRID symbol"@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "PERSON: Bill Hogan"@en,
                        "PERSON: Bjoern Peters"@en,
                        "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            iao:0000118 "looking up a CRID";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "looking up a centrally registered identifier"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000577 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
