iao:0000634 iao:0000111 "notes section"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The section labelled 'notes' in a typical scientific journal article, e.g. McLean et al. Br J Gen Pract. 2014 Jul; 64(624): e440–e447 (http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4073730/):"@en;
            iao:0000115 "A part of a document containing typically short notes about the document itself and/or the authors. Often the notes section contains subsections related to funding, competing interests, ethical approval, etc."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Bill Baumgartner"@en;
            iao:0000118 "notes"@en,
                        "footnotes"@en;
            iao:0000233 <https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/183>;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "notes section"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000314.
iao:0000635 iao:0000111 "patients section"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The section labelled 'patients' in a typical scientific journal article, e.g. in Citak et al. Acta Orthop. 2013 Jun; 84(3): 326–327. (http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3715825/)"@en;
            iao:0000115 "A part of a document about the patients that participated in a study."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Bill Baumgartner"@en;
            iao:0000233 <https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/183>;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "patients section"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000636 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000051 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            iao:0000314.
iao:0000636 iao:0000111 "patients textual entity"@en;
            iao:0000112 """Excerpt from Citak et al. Acta Orthop. 2013 Jun; 84(3): 326–327. (http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3715825/):

Between January 1996 and February 2012, we treated 4 patients with interprosthetic femoral fractures (3 of them women) (Figure 2) using a custom-made interposition device (Waldemar Link GmbH, Hamburg, Germany) (Figure 1). Mean age was 74 (59–86) years. The fractures occurred mean 18 (13–28) years after primary THA and mean 14 (10–17) years after primary TKA. At the latest follow-up, after mean 8 (0.5–16) years, revision surgery with a total femur replacement was required in 1 case due to aseptic loosening. No other complications requiring revision surgery occurred."""@en;
            iao:0000115 "A textual entity expressing information regarding the patients used in a study."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Bill Baumgartner"@en;
            iao:0000233 <https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/183>;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "patients textual entity"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000300.
iao:0000637 iao:0000111 "pre-publication history section"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The section labelled 'pre-publication history' in a typical scientific journal article, e.g. in Xiao et al. BMC Anesthesiol. 2013; 13: 33. (http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4016475/)"@en;
            iao:0000115 "A part of the document about the publication history of a document. This section typically details dates of document submission to a journal and dates of any re-submissions as well as reviewer comments and responses to reviewers by the authors."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Bill Baumgartner"@en;
            iao:0000118 "pre-publication history"@en,
                        "notice of republication"@en;
            iao:0000233 <https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/183>;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "pre-publication history section"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000638 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000051 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            iao:0000314.
iao:0000638 iao:0000111 "pre-publication history textual entity"@en;
            iao:0000112 """From Xiao et al. BMC Anesthesiol. 2013; 13: 33. (http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4016475/):

The pre-publication history for this paper can be accessed here:
http://www.biomedcentral.com/1471-2253/13/33/prepub"""@en;
            iao:0000115 "A textual entity that expresses the pre-publication history (submission dates, reviewer comments, etc) for a document, often including a hyperlink to a web page detailing the information."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Bill Baumgartner"@en;
            iao:0000233 <https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/183>;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "pre-publication history textual entity"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000300.
iao:0000639 iao:0000111 "related work section"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The section labelled 'related work' in a typical scientific journal article, e.g. Žitnik and Zupan. Bioinformatics. 2015 Jun 15; 31(12): i230–i239. (http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4542780/)"@en;
            iao:0000115 "A part of a document about work in other publications that is relevant to the content of the document."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Bill Baumgartner"@en;
            iao:0000118 "related work"@en,
                        "related literature"@en;
            iao:0000233 <https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/183>;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "related work section"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000314,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000640 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000051 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
iao:0000640 iao:0000111 "related work textual entity"@en;
            iao:0000112 """Excerpt from Žitnik and Zupan. Bioinformatics. 2015 Jun 15; 31(12): i230–i239. (http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4542780/):

Our work presented here is similar in spirit to our recently developed methodology for data fusion via collective matrix factorization (Žitnik and Zupan, 2015).

"""@en;
            iao:0000115 "A textual entity that discusses work from other publications and expresses their relevancy to the content of a document."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Bill Baumgartner"@en;
            iao:0000233 <https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/183>;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "related work textual entity"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000300.
iao:0000641 iao:0000111 "requirements section"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The section labelled 'availability and requirements' in a typical scientific journal article, e.g. Qi et al. BMC Bioinformatics. 2014; 15: 11. (http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3897912/)."@en;
            iao:0000115 "A part of a document about a resource described in the document, e.g. software, that describes the requirements necessary to use the resource, e.g. operating systems, hardware, etc. in the case of a software resource."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Bill Baumgartner"@en;
            iao:0000118 "requirements"@en;
            iao:0000233 <https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/183>;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "requirements section"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000314,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000642 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000051 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
iao:0000642 iao:0000111 "requirements textual entity"@en;
            iao:0000112 """From Qi et al. BMC Bioinformatics. 2014; 15: 11. (http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3897912/):

• Operating systems: Platform independent

• Programming language: Matlab, R, Python

• Other requirements: None

• License: GNU GPL v3

• Any restrictions to use by non-academics: None"""@en;
            iao:0000115 "A textual entity that expresses the requirements necessary to use a resource, e.g. software."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Bill Baumgartner"@en;
            iao:0000233 <https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/183>;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "requirements textual entity"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000300.
iao:0000643 iao:0000111 "statistical analysis textual entity"@en;
            iao:0000112 """From Mondo et al. Cardiovasc J Afr. 2013 Mar; 24(2): 28–33. (http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3734881/):

Data were captured into EPI-DATA (version 3.1), cleaned and then exported to Stata version 10 for analysis. Continuous variables were summarised as mean (± standard deviation) and median (inter-quartile range), and presented in the tables. Categorical data were analysed using frequency and percentages, and results are presented in frequency tables and bar charts. Test of significance (p-value) was determined using the chi-square test. A p-value of less than 0.05 was considered significant."""@en;
            iao:0000115 "A textual entity documenting statistical analysis tools and techniques employed."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Bill Baumgartner"@en;
            iao:0000233 <https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/183>;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "statistical analysis textual entity"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000300.
iao:0000644 iao:0000111 "statistical analysis section"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The section labelled 'statistical analysis' in a typical scientific journal article, e.g. Mondo et al. Cardiovasc J Afr. 2013 Mar; 24(2): 28–33. (http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3734881/)"@en;
            iao:0000115 "A part of the document used to describe the statistical methodologies employed in the work presented in the document."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Bill Baumgartner"@en;
            iao:0000118 "statistical analysis"@en;
            iao:0000233 <https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/183>;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "statistical analysis section"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000314,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000643 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000051 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
iao:0000645 iao:0000111 "tables section"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The section labelled 'tables' in a typical scientific journal article."@en;
            iao:0000115 "A part of a document that contains one or more tables."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Bill Baumgartner"@en;
            iao:0000118 "tables"@en;
            iao:0000233 <https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/183>;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "tables section"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000306 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000051 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            iao:0000314.
iao:0000650 iao:0000111 "database extract, transform, and load process"@en;
            iao:0000115 "A planned process which takes as input a database and fills another database by extracting concretizations of information entities from the first, transforming them, and loading the transformed concretizations into the second."@en;
            iao:0000116 "Alan Ruttenberg 12/21/16: We don't define database in IAO, currently, as the bare word is ambiguous. Reasonable interpretations of the word might be the material entity, an information structure, an information content entity. However this definition commits, at least, to there being some material thing which bear concretizations of information entities and that there are new concretizations created during the process.  We consider the ETL process in terms of information entities rather than the concretizations. No committment is made as to whether the specified output."@en,
                        "Alan Ruttenberg 12/21/16: Maybe this definition instead: A planned process which takes as input a database and copies concretizations from the first, optionally transforms then copies the result to the second";
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Alan Ruttenberg";
            iao:0000118 "ETL"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extract,_transform,_load";
            iao:0000233 <https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO/issues/187>;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/IAO>;
            rdfs:label "database extract, transform, and load process"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000030 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000011,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000030 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction];
            foaf:page <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extract,_transform,_load>.
iao:0010000 iao:0000111 "has axiom id"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Person:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            iao:0000119 "Person:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            iao:0000600 "A URI that is intended to be unique label for an axiom used for tracking change to the ontology. For an axiom expressed in different languages, each expression is given the same URI"@en;
            a owl:AnnotationProperty;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy pobo:iao.owl;
            rdfs:label "has axiom label"@en.
