obi:0000338 iao:0000111 "interpreting data";
            iao:0000112 "Concluding that a gene is upregulated in a tissue sample based on the band intensity in a western blot.  Concluding that a patient has a infection based on measurement of an elevated body temperature and reported headache. Concluding that there were problems in an investigation because data from PCR and microarray are conflicting. Concluding that 'defects in gene XYZ cause cancer due to improper DNA repair' based on data from experiments in that study that gene XYZ is involved in DNA repair, and the conclusion of a previous study that cancer patients have an increased number of mutations in this gene. ";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A planned process in which data gathered in an investigation is evaluated in the context of existing knowledge with the objective to generate more general conclusions or to conclude that the data does not allow one to draw general conclusion"@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Jennifer Fostel",
                        "PERSON: Bjoern Peters";
            iao:0000119 "Bjoern Peters";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "drawing a conclusion based on data"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0001909 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000011,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000027 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0000339 iao:0000111 "planning";
            iao:0000112 """The process of a scientist thinking about and deciding what reagents to use as part of a protocol for an experiment. Note that the scientist could be human or a \"robot scientist\" executing software.""";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "a process of creating or modifying a plan specification"@en;
            iao:0000116 "7/18/2011 BP: planning used to itself be a planned process. Barry Smith pointed out that this would lead to an infinite regression, as there would have to be a plan to conduct a planning process, which in itself would be the result of planning etc. Therefore, the restrictions on 'planning' were loosened to allow for informal processes that result in an 'ad hoc plan '. This required changing from 'has_specified_output some plan specifiction' to 'has_participant some plan specification'. ";
            iao:0000117 "Bjoern Peters";
            iao:0000119 "Bjoern Peters",
                        "Plans and Planned Processes Branch";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "planning"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000015,
                            [owl:intersectionOf (pobo:BFO_0000015
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000104 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000057 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class].
obi:0000340 iao:0000111 "obsolete_documenting";
            iao:0000112 "Recording the current temperature in a laboratory notebook. Writing a journal article. Updating a patient record in a database.";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000116 "6/11/9: Edited at workshop. Should go into IAO. We need to be able identify a child form of information artifact which corresponds to something enduring (not brain like). This used to be restricted to physical document or digital entity as the output, but that excludes e.g. an audio cassette tape";
            iao:0000117 "Bjoern Peters";
            iao:0000119 "wikipedia http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Documenting";
            iao:0000231 iao:0000228;
            iao:0100001 "IAO_0000572";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "obsolete_documenting"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf oboinowl:ObsoleteClass;
            owl:deprecated true.
obi:0000341 iao:0000111 "histological sample preparation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "histological sample preparation is the preparation of an input tissue via slicing and labeling to make tissue microstructure of interest visible in a future histology assay"@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Bjoern Peters"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OBI branch derived"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "histological sample preparation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000094,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0400168 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000057 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000456 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0100066 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000684 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000659.
obi:0000343 iao:0000111 "inductive reasoning";
            iao:0000112 "Based on the observation that all lung cancer patients treated with aspirin in our clinical trial survived longer than the control group, we conclude by inductive reasining that aspirin has a therapeutic effect on lung cancer."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000428;
            iao:0000115 "a interpreting data that is used to ascribe properties or relations to types based on an observation instance (i.e., on a number of observations or experiences); or to formulate laws based on limited observations of recurring phenomenal patterns."@en;
            iao:0000116 """BP: 10/22/122: After changing the parent class to drawing a conclusion *based on data* it is no longer clear that this class is needed; minimally it needs a better definition to distinguish it. 

Proposal is to obsolete. 

""";
            iao:0000117 "Bjoern Peters";
            iao:0000119 "wikipedia: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inductive_reasoning";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "inductive reasoning"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000338.
obi:0000345 iao:0000111 "mass analyzer"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The mass analyzer of the Voyager-DE(tm) STR Biospectrometry Workstation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A Mass analyzer is a device that separates ions according to their mass-to-charge ratio. All mass spectrometers are based on dynamics of charged particles in electric and magnetic fields in vacuum where the two laws of Lorentz force law and Newton's second law of motion apply."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson",
                        "PERSON: Daniel Schober";
            iao:0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mass_spectrometry#Mass_analyzer";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "mass analyzer"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000932,
                            obi:0000832,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000453 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000372 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0000355 iao:0000111 "hypothesis driven investigation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "is an investigation with the goal to test one or more hypothesis"@en;
            iao:0000117 "PlanAndPlannedProcess Branch"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OBI branch derived"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "hypothesis driven investigation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000066.
obi:0000356 iao:0000111 "hypothesis generating investigation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "is an investigation in which data is generated and analyzed with the purpose of generating new hypothesis"@en;
            iao:0000117 "PlanAndPlannedProcess Branch"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OBI branch derived"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "hypothesis generating investigation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000066.
obi:0000361 iao:0000111 "ion source"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The ion source of a Voyager-DE??? STR Biospectrometry Workstation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 """An ion source is a device that is part of a mass
spectrometer that ionizes the material under analysis. The ions are
then transported by magnetic or electric fields to the mass analyzer.
Techniques for ionization have been key to determining what types of
samples can be analyzed by mass spectrometry. Electron ionization and
chemical ionization are used for gases and vapors. In chemical
ionization sources, the material is ionized by chemical ion-molecule
reactions during collisions in the source. Two techniques often used
with liquid and solid biological samples include electrospray
ionization (due to John Fenn PMID 2675315.) and matrix-assisted laser
desorption/ionization (MALDI, due to M. Karas and F. Hillenkamp
(Measuring Mass: From Positive Rays to Proteins by Michael A. Grayson
(Editor) (ISBN 0-941901-31-9)))."""@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson";
            iao:0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mass_spectrometry#Ion_source";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "ion source"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000385 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000968.
obi:0000364 iao:0000111 "ion detector"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The ion detector of the Voyager-DE(tm) STR Biospectrometry Workstation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 """An ion detector is a device that measures and records
the charge induced or current produced when an ion passes by or hits a
surface. 

Example: In a scanning instrument the signal produced in the detector
during the course of the scan versus where the instrument is in the
scan (at what m/Q) will produce a mass spectrum, a record of ions as a
function of m/Q."""@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson";
            iao:0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mass_spectrometry#Detector";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "ion detector"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000453 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000832.
obi:0000365 iao:0000111 "obsolete_results_from";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000116 """2009/11/23: BP, dev call:o bsoleted as discussed in tracker https://sourceforge.net/tracker/?func=detail&aid=2899860&group_id=177891&atid=886178
. Should be replaced by instead creating defined classes for materials, which are specified output of the process that conveys the""";
            iao:0000231 iao:0000103;
            a owl:ObjectProperty;
            rdfs:label "obsolete_results_from";
            rdfs:subPropertyOf oboinowl:ObsoleteProperty;
            owl:deprecated true.
obi:0000366 iao:0000111 "metabolite profiling assay";
            iao:0000112 "Metabolite profiling of human colon carcinoma - deregulation of TCA cycle and amino acid turnover. Mol Cancer. 2008 Sep 18;7(1):72. PMID: 18799019";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An assay that detects and identifies chemical entities resulting from biochemical and cellular metabolism";
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra";
            iao:0000118 "metabolite assay";
            iao:0000119 "OBI";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "metabolite profiling assay";
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000070,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0100051 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0000367 iao:0000111 "light emission function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A light emission function is an excitation function to excite a material to a specific excitation state that it emits light."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Daniel Schober",
                        "Frank Gibson",
                        "Bill Bug",
                        "Melanie Courtot";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "light emission function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000374.
obi:0000368 iao:0000111 "record function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A record function is a function that registers or collects information in a particular format on a particular recording medium. For example on paper or a digital representation"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Bill Bug",
                        "Daniel Schober",
                        "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Frank Gibson";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "record function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000369 iao:0000111 "magnify function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A magnify function is a function to increase the size of a transmitted object image through the precise arrangement of energy diffraction elements along an imaging path."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Daniel Schober",
                        "Bill Bug",
                        "Frank Gibson";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "magnify function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000370 iao:0000111 "contain function"@en;
            iao:0000112 "A syringe, a beaker";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A contain function is a function to constrain a material entities location in space"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson",
                        "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Bill Bug",
                        "Daniel Schober";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "contain function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000371 iao:0000111 "heat function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A heat function is a function that increases the internal kinetic energy of a material"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Bill Bug",
                        "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Daniel Schober",
                        "Frank Gibson";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "heat function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000372 iao:0000111 "material separation function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A material separation function is a function that increases the resolution between two or more material entities. The  to distinction between the entities is usually based on some associated physical quality."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Bill Bug",
                        "Daniel Schober",
                        "Frank Gibson";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "material separation function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000373 iao:0000111 "ionize process";
            iao:0000112 "Electrospray ionization in mass spectrometry";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "a physical process of converting an atom or molecule into an ion by adding or removing charged particles such as electrons or other ions. This excludes chemical processes of dissociation.";
            iao:0000116 "2009-11-10. Tracker: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ionize";
            iao:0000117 "Person:Bjoern Peters";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "ionize process"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000385 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000055 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000094,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom pobo:BFO_0000002 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000057 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000456 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0000374 iao:0000111 "excitation function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A excitation function is a function  to inject energy by bombarding a material with energetic particles (e.g., photons) thereby imbuing internal material components such as electrons with additional energy.  These internal, 'excited' particles may lead to the rupturing of covalent chemical bonds or may quickly relax back to there unexcited state with an exponential time course thereby locally emitting energy in the form of photons."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Bill Bug",
                        "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Daniel Schober",
                        "Frank Gibson";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "excitation function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000375 iao:0000111 "freeze function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A freeze function is a function to decrease the internal kinetic energy of a material below the freezing point of that type of material."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Daniel Schober",
                        "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Frank Gibson",
                        "Bill Bug";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "freeze function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000376 iao:0000111 "synthesizing function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A synthesizing function is a function to assemble new output materials from distinct input materials.  The output materials typically consist of chemically distinct monomeric objects or object aggregate polymers.";
            iao:0000117 "Daniel Schober",
                        "Frank Gibson",
                        "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Bill Bug";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "synthesizing function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000377 iao:0000111 "perturb function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A perturb function is a function that disrupts the normal function of a system induced through either internal or external means.  External means of perturbation include: (1) displacement fields in the physical sense - e.g., temperature change, osmotic shock, pressure change; (2) application of small molecules such as drugs or toxins to perturb the function of specific pathways or application of surfactants to perturb the normal function of plasma membrane.  Internal means of perturbation include: (1) manipulation of gene function via gene knockout or transcript knockdown via RNAi; (2) directed genetic mutation leading to minimal aa alterations that interfere with peptide function."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson",
                        "Daniel Schober",
                        "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Bill Bug";
            iao:0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perturbation_biology"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "perturb function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000378 iao:0000111 "filter function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A filter function is a function to prevent the flow of certain entities based on a quality or qualities of the entity while allowing entities which have different qualities to pass through"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "filter function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000372.
obi:0000379 iao:0000111 "mechanical function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A mechanical function is a function that is realised via mechanical work (through an certain amount of energy transferred by some force)."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson",
                        "Daniel Schober",
                        "Bill Bug",
                        "Melanie Courtot";
            iao:0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mechanical_work"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "mechanical function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000380 iao:0000111 "gas filter function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A gas filter function is a filter function which prevents the flow of solid objects, defined by specific qualities, in a gas-solid mixture"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "gas filter function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000378.
obi:0000381 iao:0000111 "liquid filter function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A liquid filter function is a filter function which prevents the flow of solid objects, defined by specific qualities, in a liquid-solid mixture"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "liquid filter function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000378.
obi:0000383 iao:0000111 "transfer function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A transfer function is a function to displace a material from one location to another."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Daniel Schober",
                        "Bill Bug",
                        "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Frank Gibson";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "transfer function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000384 iao:0000111 "electricity supply function"@en;
            iao:0000112 "the function of supplying current during a neuroscience experiment.";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An electricity supply function is an energy supply function to transfer electricity from one source to another, typically a consumer of the electricity or as a stimulus during a neuroscience experiment."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Frank Gibson",
                        "Daniel Schober";
            iao:0000118 "power supply"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "electricity supply function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000391.
obi:0000385 iao:0000111 "ionization function"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The ion source in amass spectrometer";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An ionization function is a function to physically convert an atom or molecule into an ion by adding or removing charged particles such as electrons or other ions."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Daniel Schober",
                        "Bill Bug",
                        "Frank Gibson";
            iao:0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ionization"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "ionization function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000387 iao:0000111 "cool function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A cool function is a function to decrease the internal kinetic energy of a material below the initial kinetic energy of that type of material."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Frank Gibson",
                        "Daniel Schober";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "cool function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000388 iao:0000111 "connection function"@en;
            iao:0000112 "An electricity cable";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A connection function is a function to couple two or more flow channels so that material or signals can be transported from one set of channels to another."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Bill Bug",
                        "Daniel Schober",
                        "Frank Gibson",
                        "Melanie Courtot";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "connection function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000389 iao:0000111 "isoelectric focusing device"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An isoelectric focusing device is a device in which isoelectric focusing can be performed. An isoelectric focussing device had the function to contain and control the contained environment and transfer electrical energy from a power supply to a separation medium and the charged material to be separated."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson";
            iao:0000118 "isoelectric focusing unit"@en;
            iao:0000119 "sep:00097";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "isoelectric focusing device"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000401 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0002089,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000370 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000383 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000654 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000053 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0000390 iao:0000111 "thermostatic circulator"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A thermostatic circulator is a device which cools or heats a circulating liquid. It has the function to contain control the contained environment and transfer energy from or to the circulating liquid"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson";
            iao:0000119 "sep:00098";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "thermostatic circulator"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000370 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0002089,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000401 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0000391 iao:0000111 "energy supply function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An energy supply function is a function to supply or transfer energy from an energy source to a consumer of the energy"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "energy supply function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000392 iao:0000111 "information processor function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An information processor function is a function that converts information from one form to another, by a lossless process or an extraction process."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson";
            iao:0000118 "data processor function"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "information processor function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000453 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000051 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000455 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000051 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0000393 iao:0000111 "signal conversion function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A signal conversion function is an information processor function which transforms a signal into another type of signal. For example an analog-to-digital_converter, Ac/Ac converter, a synapse converts electrical action potentials into an intermediate chemical signal. The post synapse converts it back into an electric one passed on to the axon."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Bill Bug",
                        "Frank Gibson",
                        "Daniel Schober",
                        "Melanie Courtot";
            iao:0000118 "transduction function";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "signal conversion function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000392.
obi:0000394 iao:0000111 "blot module"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A blot module is a device which has the function to conatin and facilitate the material transfer process blotting to be realised"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson";
            iao:0000119 "sep:00092";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "blot module"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000383 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000968.
obi:0000395 iao:0000111 "signal amplification function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A signal amplification function is a signal conversion function to inject energy into an input signal so as to produce an output signal with increased differential magnitude while also seeking to minimize increases in the signal to noise ratio. For example, to produce a 0.1 KW output signal from a 1 mW RMS input signal."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Daniel Schober",
                        "Frank Gibson",
                        "Bill Bug",
                        "Melanie Courtot";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "signal amplification function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000393.
obi:0000397 iao:0000111 "image acquisition function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An image acquisition function is a function to acquire an image of a material"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "image acquisition function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:allValuesFrom obi:0001007 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000054 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000398 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000052 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000453.
obi:0000398 iao:0000111 "image acquisition device"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "An image creation device is a device which captures a digitized image of an object"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson";
            iao:0000118 "image acquisition device"@en;
            iao:0000119 "sep:00096";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "image creation device"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000832;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:intersectionOf (obi:0000968
                                                     [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000397 ; 
                                                     owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                                                     a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                 a owl:Class].
obi:0000399 iao:0000111 "solid support function";
            iao:0000112 "Taped, glued, pinned, dried or molecularly bonded to a solid support";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A solid support function is a function of a device on which an entity is kept in a defined position and prevented in its movement"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Frank Gibson",
                        "Daniel Schober";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "solid support function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000400 iao:0000111 "display function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A display function is a function to present information by translating that information through some lookup process into visual form."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Daniel Schober",
                        "Bill Bug",
                        "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Frank Gibson";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "display function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000392.
obi:0000401 iao:0000111 "environment control function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An environmental control function is a function that regulates a contained environment within specified parameter ranges. For example the control of light exposure, humidity and temperature."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Daniel Schober",
                        "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Frank Gibson",
                        "Bill Bug";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "environment control function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000034.
obi:0000403 iao:0000111 "sort function"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A sort function is a function to distinguish material components based on some associated physical quality or entity and to partition the separate components into distinct fractions according to a defined order."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Melanie Courtot",
                        "Frank Gibson",
                        "Daniel Schober";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "sort function"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000372.
obi:0000404 iao:0000111 "gel dryer"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A gel dryer is a device which has the function to contain and to control the contained environment to facilitate the drying of gels"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson";
            iao:0000119 "sep:00094";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "gel dryer"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000401 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0002089,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000370 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0000405 iao:0000111 "primer role";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "a complementary nucleotide probe role which inheres in nucleic acid molecular entity and is realized by the use of the entity bearing the role to initiate chain elongation.";
            iao:0000119 "(cell and molecular biology) A short strand of RNA that is synthesized along single-stranded DNA during replication, initiating DNA polymerase-catalyzed synthesis of the complementary strand. http://www.answers.com/topic/rna-primer";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "primer role"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:allValuesFrom obi:0000415 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000054 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000857.
obi:0000406 iao:0000111 "PCR product"@en;
            iao:0000112 "PCR products are the results of amplifcation process. Detection of a PCR products is used to detect DNA and RNA.";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "is double stranded DNA that is the specified output of a polymerase chain reaction"@en;
            iao:0000116 "We are using PCR and not the written out words, as this is the most common used."@en;
            iao:0000117 "GROUP: OBI BIomaterial Branch";
            iao:0000119 "GROUP: OBI BIomaterial Branch";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "PCR product"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000809,
                            chebi:4705;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:intersectionOf (chebi:4705
                                                     [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000415 ; 
                                                     owl:onProperty obi:0000312 ; 
                                                     a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                 a owl:Class].
obi:0000407 iao:0000111 "viral RNA extraction";
            iao:0000112 "The AccuPrepTM Viral RNA Extraction Kit is designed for the rapid and convenient extraction of viral RNA from cell-free samples as serum, plasma, CSF, urine, etc - http://www.biokits.com/moreinfos.html?id=2703";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "The extraction of RNA from an input material that specifically isolates viral RNA";
            iao:0000117 "Person:Bjoern Peters";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "viral RNA extraction"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom ncbitaxon:10239 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0666666.
obi:0000409 iao:0000111 "nucleic acid template role";
            iao:0000112 "a model or standard for making comparisons; wordnet.princeton.edu/perl/webwn 19 feb 2009";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
