            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000507.
obi:0000551 iao:0000111 "needle assembly"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The needle assembly attached to the autosampler, comprises the injector needle that feeds a sample or carrier gas into the inlet"@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                        "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01065";
            iao:0000232 "chromatography device, check on definition !"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "needle assembly"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000048.
obi:0000552 iao:0000111 "reverse transcribed polymerase chain reaction";
            iao:0000112 """Harmonisation of multi-centre real-time reverse-transcribed PCR results of a candidate prognostic marker in breast cancer: an EU-FP6 supported study of members of the EORTC - PathoBiology Group.

Span PN, Sieuwerts AM, Heuvel JJ, Spyratos F, Duffy MJ, Eppenberger-Castori S, Vacher S, O'Brien K, McKiernan E, Pierce A, Vuaroqueaux V, Foekens JA, Sweep FC, Martens JW.
Eur J Cancer. 2009 Jan;45(1):74-81. PMID: 19008094""";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "reverse transcribe pcr is a process which allow amplification of cDNA during a pcr reaction while the cDNA results from a retrotranscription of messenger RNA isolated from a material entity.";
            iao:0000116 "3/21/10,  BP:Modified definition to clarify that this is not the assay, but the material transformation";
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra";
            iao:0000118 "reverse transcription polymerase chain reaction",
                        "RT-PCR";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "reverse transcribed polymerase chain reaction";
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0600058,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom [owl:intersectionOf (obi:0000415
                                                                     [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0600028 ; 
                                                                     owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0002087 ; 
                                                                     a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                                 a owl:Class] ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000051 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000406 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom chebi:33697 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0000553 iao:0000111 "Bruker Capillary LC-NMR platform"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "Capillary LC-NMR is a hyphenated technique coupling capillary liquid chromatography and NMR, which increases sensitivity dramatically through the use of miniaturization of the chromatographic techniques and NMR detection volume. LC-NMR hyphenated systems separate a mixture into its pure components and couple the output to NMR for automatic sample analysis. The ever increasing need to measure lower sample amounts and lower level impurities demands the highest NMR sensitivity. Traditional LC-NMR systems with relatively large peak volumes are not optimized for such low levels of detection. Bruker BioSpin, together with Waters and Protasis has developed a Capillary LC-NMR system. The latest capillary LC attributes and highest capillary flow probe sensitivity combine with state of the art NMR systems technology. Greater mass sensitivity and faster spectral analysis with smaller sample volumes is possible. This system is ideal for analysis of metabolites and impurities associated with the drug development process."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400279",
                        "WEB:<http://www.bruker-biospin.com/hyphenation_caplcnmr.html>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en,
                        "hyphenated NMR instrument platform";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Bruker Capillary LC-NMR platform"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000596.
obi:0000554 iao:0000111 "gas chromatography oven"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A gas chromatography oven is an oven with a heated connection between the GC and the MS instrument in a GCMS-analysis, that keeps compounds in the gas phase as they leave the GC oven."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                        "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01039";
            iao:0000232 "gas chromatography equipment"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "gas chromatography oven"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000542.
obi:0000555 iao:0000111 "autosampler"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An optional part of an NMR instrument used to hold samples prior to NMR analysis and that sequentially loads these samples into the analytical part of the NMR instrument. \\n   alt The autosampler is an automatic sample changer device."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                        "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400002";
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "autosampler"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000968.
obi:0000556 iao:0000111 "isocratic pump system"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A pump system optimized for isocratic chromatography."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01049",
                        "WEB:<http://www.buchi.com/Isocratic-Pump-System.253.0.html>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "isocratic pump system"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000589.
obi:0000557 iao:0000111 "flash pump system"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "Any pump system used in flash column chromatography to push the solvent through the column. Better flow rates can be achieved by using a pump or by using compressed gas (e.g. air, nitrogen, or argon) to push the solvent through the column (flash column chromatography)."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01048",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "flash pump system"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000589.
obi:0000558 iao:0000111 "Varian UNITY INOVA spectrometer"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The UNITY INOVA is also the easiest spectrometer to use and is also the choice of those interested in using advanced NMR techniques in their own research, but without becoming, or hiring, an NMR expert. A complete set of turnkey operating environments is available for the UNITY INOVA covering the structure and dynamics of biological macromolecules, small molecules, solids, and imaging. These packages put the combined NMR expertise of the entire Varian NMR community at your fingertips."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB:<http://www.varianinc.com/cgi-bin/nav?products/NMR/spectromet/inova/index&cid=HFIH>"@en,
                        "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400236";
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Varian UNITY INOVA spectrometer"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000611.
obi:0000559 iao:0000111 "liquid NMR probe"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An NMR probe that is designed to hold a liquid sample."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400242",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR device"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "liquid NMR probe"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000516.
obi:0000560 iao:0000111 "ion exchange column"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An ion exchange column is a chromatography column that is used in ion exchange chromatography and anion or cation exchange resins to enable separation."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01105",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "ion exchange column"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000038.
obi:0000561 iao:0000111 "Bruker NMR probe"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An NMR probe that is manufactured by Bruker."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                        "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400231";
            iao:0000232 "NMR device, TODO: May need no definition."@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Bruker NMR probe"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000516.
obi:0000562 iao:0000111 "anion trap column"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An anion trap column is a trap column and ion-exchange column which contains cationic anion-exchange resins."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01277",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "anion trap column"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000518.
obi:0000563 iao:0000111 "fluorescene detector"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A single wavelength detector, where the excitation light wavelength is normally a mercury lamp generated high intensity UV light at 253.7 nm. Many substances that fluoresce will be excited by light of this wavelength and hence be detected."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01080",
                        "WEB:<http://www.chromatography-online.org/HPLC-Detectors/Fluorescence/Single-Wavelength-Excitation/rs57.html>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "fluorescene detector"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000832,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000453 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0000564 iao:0000111 "tecmag EAGLE probe"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The Eagle is a 4 mm 1H/X solid-state MAS probe with a top spinning speed of 18 kHz. Its simple design is robust, reliable and easy to spin. Configurations are available for 200 to 600 MHz wide bore magnets on Tecmag, Bruker, Chemagnetics, JEOL and Varian spectrometers."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                        "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400248";
            iao:0000232 "NMR probe"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "tecmag EAGLE probe"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000479.
obi:0000565 iao:0000111 "electrical conductivity detector"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The electrical conductivity detector measures the conductivity of the mobile phase. There is usually background conductivity which must be backed-off by suitable electronic adjustments. If the mobile phase contains buffers, the detector gives a base signal that completely overwhelms that from any solute usually making detection impossible. Thus, the electrical conductivity detector a bulk property detector. and senses all ions whether they are from a solute or from the mobile phase. In order to prevent polarization of the sensing electrodes, AC voltages must be used and so it is the impedance not the resistance of the electrode system that is actually measured. From a physical chemistry stand point the conductivity of a solution is more important than its resistance. However, it is the resistance (impedance) of the electrode system that determines the current across it. The resistance of any conductor varies directly as its length and inversely as its cross sectional area."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01239",
                        "WEB:<http://www.chromatography-online.org/HPLC-Detectors/Electrical-Conductivity/rs83.html>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "electrical conductivity detector"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000832,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000453 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0000566 iao:0000111 "NMR instrument"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An Instrument which is used to carry out a NMR analysis of some sample."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000118 "NMR instrument"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400059",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "NMR instrument"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000453 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000832.
obi:0000567 iao:0000111 "Bruker UltraShield NMR magnet"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An NMR magnet manufactured by Bruker that ensures field homogeneity without amplified effects from vibrations or thermal changes. This magnet technology uses active shielding and optimizes coil design."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400187",
                        "WEB:<http://www.bruker-biospin.com/nmr_magnets_us.html?&print=http%3A%2Fitsupportunit.com%2Fawstats%2Ficon%2Fnisum%2Fivuj%2F>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Bruker UltraShield NMR magnet"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000597.
obi:0000568 iao:0000111 "piston-seal"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The seal made by a piston in a diaphragm pump. The unique property of the reciprocating diaphragm pump is that the actuating piston does not come into direct contact with the mobile phase and thus, the demands on the piston-cylinder seal are not so great. The diaphragm has a relatively high surface area and thus, the movement of the diaphragm is relatively small and consequently the pump can be operated at a fairly high frequency. High frequency pumping results in a very significant reduction in pulse amplitude and, in addition, high frequency pulses are more readily damped by the column system. Nevertheless, it must be emphasized that diaphragm pumps are not pulseless."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01116",
                        "WEB:<http://www.chromatography-online.org/HPLC/Basic-HPLC/Pump/Diaphragm/rs15.html>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "piston-seal"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000601.
obi:0000569 iao:0000111 "mass selective detector"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A mass selective detector is a GC detector that uses mass spectrometry. It is based upon the ionization of solute molecules in the ion source and the separation of the ions generated on the basis of their mass/charge ratio by an analyzer unit. This may be a magnetic sector analyzer, a quadruple mass filter, or an ion trap. Ions are detected by a dynode electron multiplier."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000118 "mass spectrometry detector"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB:<http://homepages.onsnet.nu/%7Ealkema/html/whatisgc.html>"@en,
                        "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01198";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "mass selective detector"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000637.
obi:0000570 iao:0000111 "spin column"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A spin column is a chromatography column which is suitable for putting it into a centrifuge. A spin column enforces separation through increased G-forces while spinning the column in a centrifuge. It is often used in DNA gel extraction kits."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01232",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "spin column"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000038.
obi:0000571 iao:0000111 "manufacturer role";
            iao:0000112 "With respect to The Accuri C6 Flow Cytometer System, the organization Accuri bears the role manufacturer role.  With respect to a transformed line of tissue culture cells derived by a specific lab, the lab whose personnel isolated the cll line bears the role manufacturer role.  With respect to a specific antibody produced by an individual scientist, the scientist who purifies, characterizes and distributes the anitbody bears the role manufacturer role.";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "Manufacturer role is a role which inheres in a person or organization and which is realized by a manufacturing process.";
            iao:0000117 "GROUP:  Role Branch";
            iao:0000119 "OBI";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "manufacturer role";
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom [owl:unionOf (ncbitaxon:9606
                                                              obi:0000245) ; 
                                                 a owl:Class] ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000052 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:allValuesFrom obi:0000457 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000054 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            pobo:BFO_0000023.
obi:0000572 iao:0000111 "transfer line"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A combination of devices that are used in connection with a sampling head for transferring components of an applied sample to the analyzing part of a chromatography system."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01235",
                        "WEB:<http://www.freepatentsonline.com/5702671.html>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "chromatography device"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "transfer line"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000048.
obi:0000573 iao:0000111 "gradient pump system"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A pump system optimized for gradient chromatography."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01050",
                        "WEB:<http://www.buchi.com/Gradient-Pump-System.531.0.html>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "gradient pump system"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000589.
obi:0000574 iao:0000111 "high temperature column"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A high temperature column is a chromatography column which is suitable for and withstands very high temperatures in chromatography ovens."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01233",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "high temperature column"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000038.
obi:0000575 iao:0000111 "Bruker Ultrastabilized NMR magnet"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An NMR magnet manufactured by Bruker for Ultra-High Field NMR, available from 750 MHz to 900 MHz, which provides reliable operation at reduced temperature and ambient pressure via being rigidly mounted and stabilized."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400188",
                        "WEB:<http://www.bruker-biospin.com/nmr_magnets_ultrastabilized.html?&print=http%3A%2Fitsupportunit.com%2Fawstats%2Ficon%2Fnisum%2Fivuj%2F>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Bruker Ultrastabilized NMR magnet"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000597.
obi:0000576 iao:0000111 "scattered molecular aggregate";
            iao:0000112 "the sodium and chloride ions in a glass of salt water";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "a material entity that consists of all the molecules of a specific type that are located in some bounded region and which is part of a more massive material entity that has parts that are other such aggregates"@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            iao:0000118 "Collective"@en;
            iao:0000119 "Discussion in Karslruhe with, among others, Alan Rector, Stefan Schulz, Marijke Keet, Melanie Courtot, and Alan Ruttenberg. With inspiration from the paper Granularity, scale and collectivity: When size does and does not matter, Alan Recto, Jeremy Rogers, Thomas Bittner, Journal of Biomedical Informatics 39 (2006) 333-349"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "scattered molecular aggregate"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:allValuesFrom chebi:23367 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000643 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom chebi:23367 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000643 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            pobo:BFO_0000040.
obi:0000577 iao:0000111 "molecular concentration";
            iao:0000112 "the phosphate concentration should be 0.1M";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A concentration is a relational quality that inheres in a material entity towards molecular scattered aggregate that is part of it by virtue of some ratio of masses of the two or the counts of the grains of the two or volume occupied by the larger material entity.";
            iao:0000116 """JZ: Can we replace the term by PATO:
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000033
If not, we will wait the term available in PATO.

Although specified that obsolete reason is 'term imported', the term has not imported yet. Will keep tracking this term until import the replaced term.

Term depracted since the object property 'towards' used in the axioms is not avaliable in BFO2. """,
                        """This term represent a quality of molecular concentration. If there is need for some other sort of concentration - e.g. ratio of counts of cells, another term is needed. 

OBI uses a standard unit for representing concentration qualities but this still needs to be decided on. A relation needs to be defined that relates the quality instance to the representation of its quantitative value in the chosen units. See http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Concentration

Measurements of concentration may be in any appropriate unit. Note that precise concentrations are virtually never known.

Finally, note that there is no such thing as a concentration of 0. A concentration is a *relational* quality and so can't exist unless both entities it inheres in exist. However one map make concentration measurements that turn out not to be about concentrations qualities, if it happens that the scattered molecular aggregate doesn't actually exist.""",
                        """logical definition in OBI:
  'quality of related physical entities'
  ('inheres in' some material_entity) and (towards some 'scattered molecular aggregate')""";
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg";
            iao:0000119 "Discussion in Karslruhe, Oct 2008, with, among others, Alan Rector, Stefan Schulz, Marijke Keet, Melanie Courtot, and Alan Ruttenberg.";
            iao:0000231 iao:0000228;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "obsolete_molecular concentration"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf oboinowl:ObsoleteClass;
            owl:deprecated true.
obi:0000578 iao:0000111 "NMR sample tube"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The sample-tube holds the NMR sample and sits in the nmr probe. It is usually a glass tube of 5-20mm diameter."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400132",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR device"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "NMR sample tube"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000566 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000050 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000836.
obi:0000579 iao:0000111 "Varian UNITY spectrometer"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The predecessor series of the Varian UNITY INOVA spectrometer."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB:<http://www.scs.uiuc.edu/NMR/instruments/u400.php>"@en,
                        "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400237";
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Varian UNITY spectrometer"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000611.
obi:0000580 iao:0000111 "AVANCE II spectrometer"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A spectrometer suitable for metabolomics and in vivo NMR studies but structural analysis of small molecules and low molecular weight proteins can also be performed. To accomplish these studies there are six probe-heads available. A successor, the AVANCE III came out recently."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400197",
                        "WEB:<http://cermax.itqb.unl.pt/mambo/en/index.php?option=com_content&task=view&id=36&Itemid=93>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "AVANCE II spectrometer"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000596.
obi:0000581 iao:0000111 "y-column connector"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A column connector that connects one column on one side with two columns at the other side, hence building a Y shaped structure."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01237",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "y-column connector"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000478.
obi:0000582 iao:0000111 "Bruker LC-NMR/MS platform"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "Includes the connection to a high-resolution TOF-LC-MS system."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                        "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400277";
            iao:0000232 "hyphenated NMR instrument platform",
                        "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Bruker LC-NMR/MS platform"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000596.
obi:0000583 iao:0000111 "refractive index detector"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "For analyzing non-UV absorbing substances, such as carbohydrates, lipids and polymers. This is also the detector of choice for gel permeation chromatography. The refractive index detector is one of the least sensitive LC detectors. It is very sensitive to changes in ambient temperature, pressure changes, flow-rate changes and can not be used for gradient elution. Despite these many disadvantages, this detector is extremely useful for detecting those compounds that are nonionic, do not adsorb in the UV, and do not fluoresce. There are many optical systems used in refractive index detectors but one of the most common is the differential refractive index detector."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB:<http://www.chromatography-online.org/HPLC/Refractive-Index/rs33.html>"@en,
                        "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01081";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "refractive index detector"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000453 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000832.
obi:0000584 iao:0000111 "anion exchange column"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An anion exchange column is a chromatography column that is used in anion exchange chromatography and which enables the separation of anion mixtures."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01095",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "anion exchange column"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000560.
obi:0000586 iao:0000111 "plunger column"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A plunger column is a chromatography column with adjustable heigth control. By means of an adjustable endpiece (plunger) the user can adjust the column length without disturbing the packed bed. Plunger columns can equalize volume changes and thus avoids dead volumes within the column."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01108",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "plunger column"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000038.
obi:0000588 iao:0000111 "flame photometric detector"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The determination of sulfur or phosphorus containing compounds is the job of the flame photometric detector (FPD). This device uses the chemiluminescent reactions of these compounds in a hydrogen/air flame as a source of analytical information that is relatively specific for substances containing these two kinds of atoms. The emitting species for sulfur compounds is excited S2. The lambda max for emission of excited S2 is approximately 394 nm. The emitter for phosphorus compounds in the flame is excited HPO (lambda max = doublet 510-526 nm). In order to selectively detect one or the other family of compounds as it elutes from the GC column, an interference filter is used between the flame and the photomultiplier tube (PMT) to isolate the appropriate emission band. The drawback here being that the filter must be exchanged between chromatographic runs if the other family of compounds is to be detected."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000118 "FPD"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01091",
                        "WEB:<http://www.shsu.edu/~chemistry/FPD/FPD.html>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "flame photometric detector"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000637.
obi:0000589 iao:0000111 "chromatography pump system"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "Better flow rates can be achieved by using a pump or by using compressed gas (e.g. air, nitrogen, or argon) to push the solvent through the column (flash column chromatography)."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01046",
                        "WEB:<http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Column_chromatography>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "chromatography pump system"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000485.
obi:0000590 iao:0000111 "Bruker 1mm MicroProbe"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "Over the past few years there has been a significantly growing demand for miniaturization in all areas ofmodern research and development. Evoked by many exciting applications, there is a need for analytical methods which require less amounts of sample. Bruker BioSpin meets this challenge with a revolutionary NMR probe design: The 1mm MicroProbe. It operates with disposable 1mm capillary sample tubes and the sample volume of 5 microliters enables the use of lowest amounts of sample to run all high resolution NMR experiments with outstanding sensitivity and up to 16 times faster measurements. Due to the TXI-type probe design, the z-gradient coil and the automatic matching and tuning accessory, the 1mm MicroProbe can be used for a wide variety of NMR experiments. The key advantages of this probe include:\\n   up to 4 times higher mass sensitivity than 5mm conventional probes (with respect to the same sample amount)\\n   excellent solvent suppression properties\\n   virtually no salt effect\\n   discrete samples in tubes that can be sealed and stored\\n   automation accessory for sample preparation and handling available."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400194",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR probe"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Bruker 1mm MicroProbe"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000561.
obi:0000591 iao:0000111 "Bruker BEST NMR system"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The introduction of biological screening and combinatorial chemistry for chemical synthesis has also introduced new requirements for NMR automation, e.g., the use of well plates for sample input, increased demands on throughput, and the need for quick and simple interpretation of the acquired NMR data."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000118 "Bruker Efficient Sample Transfer NMR"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400206",
                        "WEB:<http://www.bruker-biospin.com/automation.html>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Bruker BEST NMR system"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000464.
obi:0000592 iao:0000111 "chromatography detector filter"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An optical filter that is used to obtain monochromatic light of a defined wavelength from detector lamps."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01121",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "chromatography detector filter"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000601.
obi:0000593 iao:0000111 "cation trap column"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A cation trap column is a trap column and ion-exchange column which contains anionic cation-exchange resins."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01278",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "cation trap column"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000518.
obi:0000594 iao:0000111 "column adapter"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An Adapter that enabled the connection of a column to additional devices."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01113",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "chromatography device"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "column adapter"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000048.
obi:0000595 iao:0000111 "pulsed amperometric detector"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A chromatography detector as used by high-performance anion exchange chromatography that provides sensitive and specific detection of carbohydrates. Pulsed Electrochemical Detection (PED) allows simple, sensitive, and direct detection of numerous polar aliphatic compounds, especially carbohydrates. This technique exploits the electrocatalytic activity of noble metal electrode surfaces to oxidize various polar functional groups. In PED, multi-step potential-time waveforms at Au and Pt electrodes realize amperometric/coulometric detection while maintaining uniform and reproducible electrode activity. The response mechanisms in PED are dominated by the surface properties of the electrode, and, as a consequence, members of each chemical class of compounds produce virtually identical voltammetric responses. Thus, the full potential is realized when combined with high performance liquid chromatography (HPLC)."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000118 "PAD"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01240",
                        "WEB:<http://adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2004SPIE.5261..103L>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "pulsed amperometric detector"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000453 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000832.
obi:0000596 iao:0000111 "Bruker NMR instrument"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An NMR instrument that is manufactured by Bruker."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                        "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400198";
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Bruker NMR instrument"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000566.
obi:0000597 iao:0000111 "Bruker NMR magnet"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An NMR magnet that is manufactured by Bruker."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400186",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Bruker NMR magnet"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000517.
obi:0000598 iao:0000111 "ozone-induced chemiluminescence detector"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "Although there are many direct ozone chemiluminescent reactions with various gaseous molecules, the incorporation of a conversion step to convert various non-chemiluminescent analytes to a species capable of reacting with ozone to produce chemiluminescence broadens the horizon of this technique tremendously. The conversion of nearly all nitrogen- and sulfur-containing compounds to their respective chemiluminescent species for universal nitrogen and sulfur detection has made nitrogen/sulfur chemiluminescence detection the most widely used analytical methods based upon ozone-induced chemiluminescence. In addition to non-chromatographic applications, nitrogen/sulfur chemiluminescence detection has been adapted to various chromatographic techniques from gas chromatography to liquid and supercritical fluid chromatography as specialized element-specific detectors. The characteristics of these detectors are evaluated and compared to other element-selective detection techniques. The unique features of the chemiluminescence detectors have made them powerful tools in many diverse fields of analytical chemistry."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01088",
                        "WEB:<http://sangerhinxtongbr.library.ingentaconnect.com/content/els/00219673/1999/00000842/00000001/art00177>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "ozone-induced chemiluminescence detector"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000637.
obi:0000599 iao:0000111 "tecmag NMR console"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An NMR console manufactured by tecmac."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                        "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400246";
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "tecmag NMR console"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000499.
obi:0000600 iao:0000111 "JEOL NMR instrument"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An NMR instrument that is manufactured by JEOL."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400226",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "JEOL NMR instrument"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000566.
obi:0000601 iao:0000111 "chromatography consumable"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A chromatography consumable is a consumable that is used in a chromatography experiment."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                        "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01115";
            iao:0000232 "chromatography device"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "chromatography consumable"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000048.
obi:0000602 iao:0000111 "column frit"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A part of the column content that separates column packing compartments. In radial columns the packing is supported between two cylindrical frits and the gap between represents the bed height or column length. The outer frit is the column inlet and consequently the sample initially has a large area of stationary phase with which to interact. Frits are porous metal products to prevent unwanted particles from entering the chromatography system. These particles may come from the sample, the solvent or debris generated by the chromatography system itself. Such particles entering the system may lead to clogging of capillaries, interference with the chromatography by changing chromatographic parameters or disturbance of the detector function. Characteristics of a frit, besides the diameter and the thickness, is the porosity (pore distribution, density)."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01070",
                        "WEB:<http://www.chromatography-online.org/topics/radial/columns.html>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "chromatography device"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "column frit"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000048.
obi:0000603 iao:0000111 "liquid chromatography column"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A liquid chromatography column is a chromatography column that is used in liquid chromatography, i.e. a column that is provided with a liquid sample mix."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01227",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "liquid chromatography column"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000038.
obi:0000604 iao:0000111 "detector lamp"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A lamp used in a chromatography detector that excites sample molecules at certain frequencies / emission wavelengths, e.g. Mercury Vapor Lamp (253.7 nm), Zinc Vapor Lamp (2123.9 nm and 307.6 nm), Cadmium Vapor Lamp (228.8, 326.1,340.3, and 346.6 nm). To obtain monochromatic light an appropriate light filter would be needed."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01119",
                        "WEB:<http://www.chromatography-online.org/HPLC/UV-Detectors/Fixed-Wavelength/rs23.html>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "detector lamp"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000601.
obi:0000605 iao:0000111 "chart recorder"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The chart recorder is a device that transduces signal-intensities into a graphical peak output: As the separated components of the gas sample emerge into the detector, the change in voltage in the detecting bridge circuit causes a representative peak to be drawn on a chart recorder. The position of the peak along the time axis of the chart measures the component's retention time, which identifies the component. This is directly related to carrier gas flow rate, temperature and column packing and dimensions. The area under each peak is proportional to the concentration of the component of the sample. The area of the peaks inscribed on the chart recorder can be determined by multiplying the height of the peak in mm, by the width of the peak in mm at 1/2 the peak height. The calibration curves for use with the chart recorder are therefore peak area plotted against concentration."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01069",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "chromatography device"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "chart recorder"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000048.
obi:0000606 iao:0000111 "open tubular column"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An open tubular column is a chromatography column in which the particles of the solid stationary phase or the support coated with a liquid stationary phase are concentrated on or along the inside tube wall leaving an open, unrestricted path for the mobile phase in the middle part of the tube."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01219",
                        "WEB:<http:www.iupac.org/publications/pac/1993/pdf/6504x0819.pdf>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "open tubular column"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000038.
obi:0000607 iao:0000111 "high resolution magic angle spin probe"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "Samples that are neither solid nor liquid, being of biological, chemical, or pharmaceutical interest, reveal highly resolved spectra when magic angle spinning is applied. The correct solution is a gradient, such that the field varies along the spinner axis. This so-called Magic Angle Gradient is employed in Brukers high resolution Magic Angle Spinning (hr-MAS) probes, and is implemented in such a way that it is compatible with the stator and does not interfere with the sample eject or insert. Bruker BioSpin has developed a series of dedicated probes for standard bore magnets to accommodate the rapidly expanding field of hr-MAS. These probes are available in double (e.g. 1H and 13C) and triple resonance (e.g. 1H, 13C, 15N) modes and come equipped with a deuterium lock channel. The probes have automatic sample ejection and insertion capability, with the availability of an optional sample changer, enabling fully automated sample runs. Probes can be equipped with an optional B0 gradient, directed along the magic angle, so that gradient spectroscopy can be done used."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000118 "high resolution MAS, hr-MAS"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400192",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR probe"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "high resolution magic angle spin probe"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000480.
obi:0000608 iao:0000111 "hydrogen generator"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A gas generator that generates hydrogen gas."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01035",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "hydrogen generator"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000507.
obi:0000609 iao:0000111 "glass column"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A glass column is a chromatography column made out of glass that is usually used for larger scale and preparative liquid chromatography separations."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01101",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "glass column"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000038.
obi:0000610 iao:0000111 "auto injector"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A gas chromatography device that can auto-inject a small number of samples an inlet."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01058",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "auto injector"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000504.
obi:0000611 iao:0000111 "Varian NMR instrument"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An NMR instrument that is manufactured by Varian."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400234",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Varian NMR instrument"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000566.
obi:0000612 iao:0000111 "Bruker MATCH tube holder system"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The Bruker Multiple Adjustable Tube Clamp Holder MATCH system is a holder for 100 mm long NMR sample tubes with diameters ranging from micro tubes up to 5 mm NMR tubes. The MATCH insert fits into a standard 10 mm Bruker spinner and is suitable for all non-spinning applications.\\n   The MATCH system provides an easy and cost efficient means of optimizing the signal-to-noise ratio of each sample. By matching the NMR tube diameter to the size of the sample, most of the sample can be placed in the active column of the NMR coil. This leads to an enhanced signal detection compared to diluting the same sample quantity in a larger tube."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000118 "Bruker Multiple Adjustable Tube Clamp Holder"@en;
            iao:0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                        "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400211";
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Bruker MATCH tube holder system"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000484.
obi:0000613 iao:0000111 "Bruker SPE-NMR platform"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A Solid Phase Extraction (SPE) system provides an interface between liquid chromatography (LC) and NMR. For the process of LC-SPE  NMR a chromatographic separation is done and the peaks of interest are trapped on an individual SPE cartridge after the column. The peak selection is done either by UV detection or by evaluation of the on-line registered MS or MSn spectra."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en,
                        "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400278";
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en,
                        "hyphenated NMR instrument platform";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Bruker SPE-NMR platform"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000596.
obi:0000614 iao:0000111 "guard column"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "Guard columns are installed between the injection valve and the analytical or preparative column and here will remove contaminants and prolong the lifetime of the columns."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01111",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "chromatography device"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "guard column"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000048.
obi:0000615 iao:0000111 "protein expression profiling assay";
            iao:0000112 "Protein Expression Profiling During Chick Retinal Maturation: A Proteomics-based approach. PMID:19077203";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An assay that determines protein expression and translation activity using protein extracts collected from a material entity.";
            iao:0000117 "Phlippe Rocca-Serra";
            iao:0000118 "proteomic analysis";
            iao:0000119 "OBI branch derived";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "protein expression profiling assay";
