obi:0000616 iao:0000111 "high resolution probe with automatic tuning and matching"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The Automatic Tuning and Matching (ATM) option for AVANCE spectrometers is available for double resonance probes in fixed-frequency and broadband tunable configurations with either direct or indirect detection. Thus, for multinuclear operation, as often required for applications in inorganic chemistry, ATM facilitates the accurate setting of 90 degree pulse widths on both observe and decoupling channels for each chosen nucleus and each individual sample - even with full automation. Triple resonance probes in fixed-frequency configurations, as typically used for inverse detection with high-field systems."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000118 "High Resolution Probes with Automatic Tuning and Matching, HR_probe_with_ATM"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400224",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR probe"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "high resolution probe with automatic tuning and matching"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000480.
obi:0000617 iao:0000111 "fluorine-induced chemiluminescence detector"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A gas chromatographic detection system based on the low pressure, gas phase chemiluminescence of the reaction mixture of molecular fluorine with organo-sulfur, -selenium, and -tellurium compounds separated from (gas phase) headspace samples. This detector was originally developed in the research group of John Birks at the University of Colorado, USA and was manufactured and sold by Sievers Instruments (Boulder Colorado, USA). This system can be divided up into three parts: the chromatograph, transfer line, and reaction cell; PMT and photon counting electronics; and the molecular fluorine generator."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01087",
                        "WEB:<http://www.shsu.edu/~chm_tgc/publications/JPP/chasteen.htm>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "fluorine-induced chemiluminescence detector"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000637.
obi:0000618 iao:0000111 "size exclusion column"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A size exclusion column is a chromatography column as used in size exclusion chromatography and which enables the separation of mixtures according to differrences in molecular size."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01100",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "size exclusion column"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000038.
obi:0000619 iao:0000111 "chromatography splitter"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An adjustable restriction that is placed in the waste outlet to allow the necessary pressure to develop at the column inlet to force a flow (q ml/min) through the column. If the flow of mobile phase is Q ml/min then the waste flow will be (Q-q) ml/min. by adjusting the waste flow, the proportion of the sample entering the capillary column can be varied over a wide range of values and the necessary minimum permissible volume for the particular column in use can be selected for analysis. Unfortunately, the fraction taken in this way may not be representative of the original sample. This is due to the individual solutes in the mixture having different diffusivities and, thus, they distribute themselves across the sampling tube in an irregular manner. In general, the components with higher diffusivities (e.g., those solutes of lower molecular weight) will diffuse away from the bulk sample more quickly than those having lower diffusivities."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01041",
                        "WEB:<http://www.chromatography-online.org/EC-Dispersion/GC-Capillary-Columns/rs13.html>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "chromatography device"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "chromatography splitter"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000048.
obi:0000620 iao:0000111 "Bruker micro imaging probe"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "For medical, biological and material sciences research, avance imaging systems provide optimal object handling and performance with a variety of samples types. Two classes of imaging probes are available: in vivo probes for handling and sustaining live objects such as animals and plants, and conventional imaging probes for materials samples."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400225",
                        "WEB:<http://www.bruker-biospin.com/probes_microimaging.html>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR probe"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Bruker micro imaging probe"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000561.
obi:0000621 iao:0000111 "custom made column"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A custom made column ia a chromatography column which is specifically tailored according to the needs of the separation as requested by a scientist or working group."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01234",
                        "GROUP:<http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "custom made column"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000038.
obi:0000622 iao:0000111 "gel permeation column"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A gel permeation column is a chromatography column which is used in gel permeation chromatography and which employs as the stationary phase a swollen gel made by polymerizing and cross-linking styrene in the presence of a diluent which is a nonsolvent for the styrene polymer. The polymer to be analyzed is introduced at the top of the column and then is elutriated with a solvent. The polymer molecules diffuse through the gel at rates depending on their molecular size."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/CHROM.owl#msi_01103",
                        "WEB:<http://composite.about.com/od/glossaries/l/bldef_g2419.htm>"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "gel permeation column"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000038.
obi:0000623 iao:0000111 "NMR spectroscopy assay";
            iao:0000112 "Metabolic profiling studies on the toxicological effects of realgar in rats by (1)H NMR spectroscopy. Wei L, Liao P, Wu H, Li X, Pei F, Li W, Wu Y. Toxicol Appl Pharmacol. 2008 Nov 25. PMID: 19073202";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "An assay that exploits the magnetic properties of certain nuclei (those with a spin) to resonate when placed in particular magnetic field conditions. Instruments recording NMR spectrum and sets of analysis can be used to deduce identity of chemical as well as composition of complex chemical mixtures.";
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra";
            iao:0000118 "Nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy";
            iao:0000119 "url:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_magnetic_resonance_spectroscopy";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "NMR spectroscopy assay";
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000070.
obi:0000624 iao:0000111 "Bruker SampleJet system"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "Bruker BioSpin introduces the SampleJet, a robot for NMR tube automation. The SampleJet has been consciously designed to meet the growing customer demand for simplicity, versatility and higher throughput in NMR sample tube automation.\\n  The SampleJet utilizes the modern-day industry standard for sample arrangements-the 96 well plate array. Therefore, the samples may be handled by standard lab automation devices before or after the NMR measurement."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400208",
                        "WEB:<http://www.bruker-biospin.com/automation.html>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Bruker SampleJet system"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000464.
obi:0000625 iao:0000111 "JEOL ECX NMR spectrometer"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The ECX series of NMR spectrometers is designed for any laboratory needing an easy-to-use, reliable, routine NMR system. The ECX NMR series is available from 300 to 500 MHz. The console is designed around a modular, digital NMR electronics chassis controlled by an intelligent acquisition computer. For unprecedented flexibility, the JEOL NMR system offers a Windows XP, Mac OSX or LINUX. Both the workstation and spectrometer may be connected to a standard network, allowing seamless remote operation anywhere in the world."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://msi-ontology.sourceforge.net/ontology/NMR.owl#msi_400227",
                        "WEB:<http://www.jeol.com/PRODUCTS/AnalyticalInstruments/NuclearMagneticResonance/ECX/tabid/145/Default.aspx>"@en;
            iao:0000232 "NMR instrument"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "JEOL ECX NMR spectrometer"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000600.
obi:0000626 iao:0000111 "DNA sequencing assay";
            iao:0000112 "Illumina (Solexa) sequencing is an example of DNA sequencing";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A sequencing assay which determines information on the sequence of a DNA molecule.";
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra";
            iao:0000118 "nucleotide sequencing";
            iao:0000119 "url:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DNA_sequencing";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "DNA sequencing assay";
