obi:0001905 iao:0000111 "secondary cultured cell population";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A cultured cell population that is derived through one or more passages in culture.";
            iao:0000116 "The term 'secondary cell culture' is generally used in biological texts/protocols to refer to any culture of cells following an initial passage.  We include it here because there are often a number of passages between a primary culture and the establishment of a stable, homogenous cell line.  Such cultures are considered to be 'secondary cultures' but not 'cell lines' during this intermediate passaging/selection period between their derivation from a 'primary cell culture' and derivation into a 'cell line', which is a more specific type of secondary culture.";
            iao:0000117 "PERSON:Matthew Brush";
            iao:0000118 "secondary cell culture sample";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON:Matthew Brush";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:comment "The concept of a 'secondary cultured cell population' covers cell lines as well as cultured cell populations more immediately derived from a primary culture which have yet to achieve adequate genetic stability and compositional homogeneity to be considered a cell line. The extent of the collection of cells in a 'secondary cultured cell population' is restricted only in that all cell members must share a propagation history (ie be derived through a common lineage of passages from an initial culture).  Secondary cultured cell populations can be under active culture, stored in a quiescent state for future use, or applied experimentally.";
            rdfs:label "secondary cultured cell population";
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0600037 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000312 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:allValuesFrom obi:0001866 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000643 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0001866 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000643 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0100060.
obi:0001906 iao:0000111 "cancer cell line";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "An immortal cell line derived from a transformed cell that was part of a malignant tumor.";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "cancer cell line";
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000867 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000312 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            pobo:CLO_0009828.
obi:0001907 iao:0000111 "immortalizing cell line transformation";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000428;
            iao:0000115 "a genetic transformation of a cell line cell with transgenic constructs intended to confer the capability for indefinite propagation in culture";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "immortalizing cell line transformation";
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom pobo:CLO_0000001 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0600043.
obi:0001908 iao:0000111 "testable hypothesis";
            iao:0000112 "that fucoidan has a small statistically significant effect on AT3 level but no useful clinical effect as in-vivo anticoagulant, a paraphrase of part of the last paragraph of the discussion section of the paper 'Pilot clinical study to evaluate the anticoagulant activity of fucoidan', by Lowenthal et. al.PMID:19696660";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An information content entity that expresses an assertion that is intended to be tested.";
            iao:0000116 """In the Philly 2013 workshop, we recognized the limitations of \"hypothesis textual entity\", and we introduced this as more general. The need for the 'textual entity' term going forward is up for future debate. 
""";
            iao:0000117 "Group:2013 Philly Workshop group";
            iao:0000118 "hypothesis";
            iao:0000119 "Group:2013 Philly Workshop group";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "testable hypothesis";
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030.
obi:0001909 iao:0000111 "conclusion based on data";
            iao:0000112 """The conclusion that a gene is upregulated in a tissue sample based on the band intensity in a western blot. The conclusion that a patient has a infection based on measurement of an elevated body temperature and reported headache. The conclusion that there were problems in an investigation because data from PCR and microarray are conflicting.
The following are NOT conclusions based on data: data themselves; results from pure mathematics, e.g. \"13 is prime\".""";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An information content entity that is inferred from data.";
            iao:0000116 """In the Philly 2013 workshop, we recognized the limitations of \"conclusion textual entity\", and we introduced this as more general. The need for the 'textual entity' term going forward is up for future debate. """;
            iao:0000117 "Group:2013 Philly Workshop group";
            iao:0000119 "Group:2013 Philly Workshop group";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "conclusion based on data";
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000027 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000124 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000338 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000312 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
