                                                     a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                 a owl:Class].
obi:0001937 iao:0000111 "has specified numeric value";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A relation between a value specification and a number that quantifies it.";
            iao:0000116 "A range of 'real' might be better than 'float'. For now we follow 'has measurement value' until we can consider technical issues with SPARQL queries and reasoning.";
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: James A. Overton";
            iao:0000119 "OBI";
            a owl:DatatypeProperty;
            rdfs:domain obi:0001933;
            rdfs:label "has specified numeric value";
            rdfs:range owl:real;
            rdfs:subPropertyOf obi:0002135.
obi:0001938 iao:0000111 "has value specification";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A relation between an information content entity and a value specification that specifies its value.";
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: James A. Overton";
            iao:0000119 "OBI";
            a owl:ObjectProperty;
            rdfs:domain iao:0000030;
            rdfs:label "has value specification";
            rdfs:range obi:0001933;
            rdfs:subPropertyOf pobo:BFO_0000051.
obi:0001939 iao:0000111 "genome coverage";
            iao:0000112 """Gigascience. 2012 Dec 27;1(1):18. doi: 10.1186/2047-217X-1-18.
PMID: 23587118. 

\"The genome coverage increased from 81.16% to 93.91%\""""@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A data item that is the total number of bases in reads, divided by genome size, assumed to be the reference size (for instance of 3.10 Gb for human and 2.73 Gb for mouse) and refers to the percentage of the genome that is contained in the assembly based on size estimates; these are usually based on cytological techniques. Genome coverage of 90–95% is generally considered to be good, as most genomes contain a considerable fraction of repetitive regions that are difficult to sequence. So it is not a cause for concern if the genome coverage of an assembly is a bit less than 100%."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Alejandra Gonzalez-Beltran"@en,
                        "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en;
            iao:0000119 """A beginner's guide to eukaryotic genome annotation. Yandell M, Ence D.
Nat Rev Genet. 2012 Apr 18;13(5):329-42. doi: 10.1038/nrg3174.
PMID: 22510764"""@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "genome coverage";
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0001872 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000312 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom pobo:SO_0001248 ; 
                             owl:onProperty iao:0000136 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            iao:0000027.
obi:0001940 iao:0000111 "N50"@en;
            iao:0000112 """Gigascience. 2012 Dec 27;1(1):18. doi: 10.1186/2047-217X-1-18.
PMID: 23587118. 

\"Here, the contig and scaffold N50 of the YH genome were ~20.9 kbp and ~22 Mbp\""""@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "the weighted median item size or N50 is a weighted median of the lengths of items, equal to the length of the longest item i such that the sum of the lengths of items greater than or equal in length to i is greater than or equal to half the length of all of the items. With regard to assemblies the items are typically contigs or scaffolds. It therefore denotes the ability of the software to create contigs and provides information about the resulting sequence assembly";
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en,
                        "Alejandra Gonzalez-Beltran"@en;
            iao:0000118 "weighted median item size"@en;
            iao:0000119 """adapted from:
\"http://genome.cshlp.org/content/21/12/2224.full?sid=74019122-f944-4ccc-bffe-d16fdd0e7d6c\"
(from table 7)
and from \"http://www.nature.com/nrg/journal/v14/n3/full/nrg3367.html\""""@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "N50"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000003 ; 
                             owl:onProperty iao:0000039 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            iao:0000032,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom pobo:SO_0001248 ; 
                             owl:onProperty iao:0000136 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0001872 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000312 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0001941 iao:0000111 "contig N50"@en;
            iao:0000112 """Gigascience. 2012 Dec 27;1(1):18. doi: 10.1186/2047-217X-1-18.
PMID: 23587118. 

\"Here, the contig and scaffold N50 of the YH genome were ~20.9 kbp and ~22 Mbp\""""@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "N50 statistic computed for the contigs produced by the assembly process. A contig N50 is calculated by first ordering every contig by length from longest to shortest. Next, starting from the longest contig, the lengths of each contig are summed, until this running sum equals one-half of the total length of all contigs in the assembly. The contig N50 of the assembly is the length of the shortest contig in this list.";
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en,
                        "Alejandra Gonzalez-Beltran"@en;
            iao:0000119 "adapted from: nature:http://www.nature.com/nrg/journal/v13/n5/box/nrg3174_BX1.html"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "contig N50"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom [owl:intersectionOf (pobo:SO_0000149
                                                                     [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0001872 ; 
                                                                     owl:onProperty obi:0000312 ; 
                                                                     a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                                 a owl:Class] ; 
                             owl:onProperty iao:0000136 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0001940.
obi:0001942 iao:0000111 "grant agency"@en;
