            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "chimera"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0100026.
obi:0100015 iao:0000111 "anatomical entity";
            iao:0000112 "Tissue, organ, system, sperm, blood or body location (arm)."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000121;
            iao:0000115 "An anatomical entity is a material entity that is part of a multicellular organism, and which is large enough so that it forms an identifiable structure in the organism. Specifically, it excludes granular parts of the organism, such as atoms, molecules, cells, which can be removed from the organism without affecting it. It is defined as the union of 'multi-tissue structure', 'body substance' and 'portion of tissue'"@en;
            iao:0000116 """equivalent classes
'portion of tissue' or 'multi-tissue structure' or 'portion of organism substance'

Superclasses
material_entity
part_of some organism""",
                        "not super happy about liquids (blood, sperm), as they seem to be 'granular' somewhat, and not form a structure."@en,
                        "10/20/09: This class and all subclasses are currently problematic. They should all be imported from other OBO foundry ontologies. (FMA / CARO / UBERON). Currently two problems exist: There is no cross species anatomy that covers all the entities we need. Secondly: there is not good boundary between anatomical entities and smaller parts in FMA. Currently we will use anatomical entities as if they are valid across species."@en,
                        """13-02-2009:
Biomaterial branch: change of label and definition following discussions at the OBI winter meeting 2009. It was felt that 'macroscopic part of multicellular organism' introduce an impractical delineation.

IMPORTANT NOTE:  OBI 'anatomical entity' would essentially correspond to FMA 'material anatomical entity' rather than FMA 'physical anatomical entity'. OBI does not include 'immaterial anatomical entity' as it would clash with the parent class 'material entity'

DOCUMENTATION NOTE: OBI anatomical entity granularity level excludes cell and biological  molecules.""",
                        """Biom call - January 2009 - Issues: 
parasites are not macroscopic part or organism. 
fetus is_a macroscopic part (but this is up for discussion)""";
            iao:0000117 "Tina Boussard"@en,
                        "Philippe Rocca-Serra",
                        "Bjoern Peters";
            iao:0000119 "MO"@en;
            iao:0000231 iao:0000228;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "obsolete_anatomical entity"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf oboinowl:ObsoleteClass;
            owl:deprecated true.
obi:0100016 iao:0000111 "blood plasma specimen"@en;
            iao:0000112 "PMID: 18217225.Sex Transm Dis. 2008 Jan;35(1):55-60. Review.Human immunodeficiency virus viral load in blood plasma and semen: review and implications of empirical findings."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "a material entity which corresponds to the liquid component of blood, in which the blood cells are suspended."@en;
            iao:0000116 "03/21/2010: BP, blood plasma is defined as the output of certain separation processes, so this is in the domain of OBI, not FMA."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "PERSON: Maura Gasparetto"@en,
                        "PERSON: Philippe Rocca-Serra";
            iao:0000118 "plasma"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood_plasma"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "blood plasma specimen"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000953,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom [owl:intersectionOf (obi:0600014
                                                                     [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000655 ; 
                                                                     owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                                                                     a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                                 a owl:Class] ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000312 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:intersectionOf (pobo:BFO_0000040
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000112 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000087 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class].
obi:0100017 iao:0000111 "blood serum specimen"@en;
            iao:0000112 "PMID: 18229666.Adv Med Sci. 2007;52 Suppl 1:204-6.Antioxidant activity of blood serum and saliva in patients with periodontal disease treated due to epilepsy."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A material entity which derives from blood and corresponds to blood plasma without fibrinogen or the other clotting factors."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Philippe Rocca-Serra",
                        "PERSON: Maura Gasparetto"@en,
                        "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood_plasma"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "blood serum specimen"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000953,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000112 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000087 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:unionOf (obi:0302885
                                                                                  obi:0302886
                                                                                  obi:0600052) ; 
                                                                     a owl:Class]
                                                                     [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000655 ; 
                                                                     owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                                                                     a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                                 a owl:Class] ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000312 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0100026 iao:0000111 "organism"@en;
            iao:0000112 "fungus"@en,
                        "animal"@en,
                        "virus"@en,
                        "plant"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A material entity that is an individual living system, such as animal, plant, bacteria or virus, that is capable of replicating or reproducing, growth and maintenance in the right environment. An organism may be unicellular or made up, like humans, of many billions of cells divided into specialized tissues and organs."@en;
            iao:0000116 """13-02-2009:
OBI doesn't take position as to  when an organism starts or ends being an organism - e.g. sperm, foetus.
This issue is outside the scope of OBI.""",
                        "10/21/09: This is a placeholder term, that should ideally be imported from the NCBI taxonomy, but the high level hierarchy there does not suit our needs (includes plasmids and 'other organisms')";
            iao:0000117 "GROUP: OBI Biomaterial Branch";
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organism"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "organism"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000040;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:unionOf (ncbitaxon:10239
                                              ncbitaxon:2
                                              ncbitaxon:2157
                                              ncbitaxon:2759) ; 
                                 a owl:Class].
