                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class].
obi:0200002 iao:0000111 "logistic-log curve fitting"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Typically used in an enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) to model the relationship between optical density (OD) and dilution. In this case a and d correspond to the theoretical OD of the assay at zero and infinite concentrations, respectively; c is the dilution associated with the point of symmetry of the sigmoid and is located at the midpoint of the assay found at the inflection point of the curve; b is a curvature parameter and is related to the slope of the curve."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A logistic-log curve fitting is a curve fitting where a curve of the form y=d+((a-d)/(1+(x/c)^b)) is obtained, where a, b, c, and d are determined so to optimize its fit to the input data points (x_1, y_1), (x_2, y_2), ..., (x_n, y_n)."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "James Malone"@en,
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "Ryan Brinkman"@en;
            iao:0000119 "ARTICLE: Plikaytis B.D. et al. (1991), J. Clin. Microbiol. 29(7): 1439-1448"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "logistic-log curve fitting"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200072,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200174 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200003 iao:0000111 "logit-log curve fitting"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Typically used in an enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) to model the relationship between optical density (OD) and dilution. In this case OD_0 (also referred to OD_min) and OD_infty (also referred to OD_max) correspond to the theoretical OD of the assay at zero and infinite concentrations, respectively."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A logit-log curve fitting is a curve fitting where first the limits y_0 an y_infty of y when x->0 and x->infinity, respectively, are estimated from the input data points (x_1, y_1), (x_2,y_2), ..., (x_n, y_n). Then a curve with equation log((y-y_0)/(y_infty-y))=a+b log(x) is obtained, where a and b are determined to optimize its fit to the input data points."@en;
            iao:0000116 "The above definition refers to the 'fully specified' logit-log model. The reduced form of this, when it is assumed that y_0=0, is named 'partially specified' logit-log model."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en,
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "Ryan Brinkman"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "ARTICLE: Plikaytis B.D. et al. (1991), J. Clin. Microbiol. 29(7): 1439-1448"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "logit-log curve fitting"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200174 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200072.
obi:0200004 iao:0000111 "log-log curve fitting"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Typically used in an enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) to model the relationship between optical density (OD) and dilution."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A log-log curve fitting is a curve fitting where first a logarithmic transformation is applied both to the x and the y coordinates of the input data points (x_1, y_1), (x_2, y_2), ..., (x_n, y_n), and then coefficients a and b are determined to optimize the fit of log(y)=a+b*log(x) to these input data points."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "Ryan Brinkman"@en,
                        "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "ARTICLE: Plikaytis B.D. et al. (1991), J. Clin. Microbiol. 29(7): 1439-1446"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "log-log curve fitting"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200174 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200072.
obi:0200005 iao:0000111 "feature extraction objective"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A feature extraction objective is a data transformation objective where the aim of the data transformation is to generate quantified values from a scanned image."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi";
            iao:0000119 "TERM: http://mged.sourceforge.net/ontologies/MGEDOntology.owl#feature_extraction"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "feature extraction objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200006 iao:0000111 "biexponential transformation"@en;
            iao:0000112 "This type of transformation is typically used in flow cytometry."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A biexponential transformation is a data transformation that, for each (one dimensional) real number input x, outputs an approximation (found, e.g. with the Newton's method) to a solution y of the equation B(y)-x=0, where B denotes a b transformation."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Joseph Spliden"@en,
                        "Ryan Brinkman"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://flowcyt.sourceforge.net/gating/latest.pdf"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "biexponential transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200072,
                            obi:0200169,
                            [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000451 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200174 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200007 iao:0000111 "box-cox transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A box-cox transformation is a data transformation according to the methods of Box and Cox as described in the article Box, G. E. P. and Cox, D.R. (1964) An analysis of transformations. Journal of Royal Statistical Society, Series B, vol. 26, pp. 211-246."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Ryan Brinkman"@en;
            iao:0000119 """ARTICLE: Box, G. E. P. and Cox, D.R. (1964), \"An analysis of transformations\", Journal of Royal Statistical Society, Series B, vol. 26, pp. 211-246."""@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "box-cox transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200169.
obi:0200008 iao:0000111 "hyperlog transformation"@en;
            iao:0000112 "This type of transformation is typically used in flow cytometry"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A hyperlog transformation ia a data transformation that, for each (one dimensional) real number input x, outputs an approximation (found, e.g. with the Newton's method) to a solution y of the equation EH(y)-x=0, where EH denotes an eh transformation."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Ryan Brinkman"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Joseph Spliden"@en;
            iao:0000119 """ARTICLE: Bagwell C.B. (2006), \"Hyperlog - a flexible log-like  transform for negative, zero, and positive valued data\", Cytometry A 64, 34-42.\""""@en,
                        "http://flowcyt.sourceforge.net/gating/latest.pdf"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "hyperlog transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200169.
obi:0200010 iao:0000111 "loess scale group transformation one-channel"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Loess scale group normalization applied to data from two one-channel expression microarray assays."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A loess scale group transformation one-channel is a loess scale group transformation consisting in the application of a scale adjustment following a loess group transformation one-channel, to render the M group variances similar."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OTHER: Editor's adjustment based on MGED Ontology term"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "loess scale group transformation one-channel"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200025.
obi:0200011 iao:0000111 "logical transformation"@en;
            iao:0000112 "This type of transformation is typically used in flow cytometry."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A logical transformation is a data transformation that, for each (one dimensional) real number input x, outputs an approximation (found, e.g. with the Newton's method) to a solution y of the equation S(y)-x=0, where S denotes an s transformation."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Ryan Brinkman"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Joseph Spliden"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://flowcyt.sourceforge.net/gating/latest.pdf"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "logical transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200169,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200012 iao:0000111 "loess scale group transformation two-channel"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Loess scale group normalization applied to data from a two-channel expression microarray assay."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A loess scale group transformation two-channel is a loess scale group transformation consisting in the application of a scale adjustment following a loess group transformation two-channel, to render the M group variances similar."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OTHER: Adjusted from MGED Ontology"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "loess scale group transformation two-channel"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200025.
obi:0200013 iao:0000111 "loess global transformation one-channel"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Loess global normalization applied to data from two one-channel expression microarray assays, where the curve is obtained using all reporters. The goal is to remove intensity-dependent biases."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A loess global transformation one-channel is a loess global transformation in the special case where the input is the result of an MA transformation applied to intensities from two related one-channel assays."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OTHER: Editor's generalization based on MGED Ontology term"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "loess global transformation one-channel"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200023.
obi:0200014 iao:0000111 "split-scale transformation"@en;
            iao:0000112 "This type of transformation is typically used in flow cytometry"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A split-scale transformation is a data transformation which is an application of a function f described as follows to a (one dimensional) real number input. f(x)=a*x+b if x=for x>t; where log denotes a logarithmic transformation and a, b, c, d, r, t are real constants, with a, c, d, r, t positive, chosen so that f is continuous with a continuous derivative at the transition point t."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Ryan Brinkman"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Joseph Spliden"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://flowcyt.sourceforge.net/gating/latest.pdf"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "split-scale transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000.
obi:0200015 iao:0000111 "loess global transformation two-channel"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Loess global normalization applied to data from a two-channel expression microarray assay, where the curve is obtained using all reporters. The goal is to remove intensity-dependent biases."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A loess global transformation two-channel is a loess global transformation in the special case where the input the result of an MA transformation applied to intensities from the two channels of a two-channel assay."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OTHER: Editor's generalization based on MGED Ontology term"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "loess global transformation two-channel"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200023.
obi:0200016 iao:0000111 "sine transformation"@en;
            iao:0000112 "sine(0)=0, sine(pi/2)=1, sine(pi)=0, sine(3*pi/2)=-1, sine(pi/6)=1/2, sine(x+2*k*pi)=sine(x) where k is any integer, etc."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A sine transformation is a data transformation which consists in applying the sine function to a (one dimensional) real number input. The sine function is one of the basic trigonometric functions and a definition is provided, e.g., at http://mathworld.wolfram.com/Sine.html."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://mathworld.wolfram.com/Sine.html"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "sine transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200169,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200017 iao:0000111 "cosine transformation"@en;
            iao:0000112 "cosine(0)=1, cosine(pi/2)=0, cosine(pi)=-1, cosine(3*pi/2)=0, cosine(pi/3)=1/2, cosine(x+2*k*pi)=cosine(x) where k is any integer, etc."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A cosine transformation is a data transformation which consists in applying the cosine function to a (one dimensional) real number input. The cosine function is one of the basic trigonometric functions and a definition is provided, e.g., at http://mathworld.wolfram.com/Cosine.html."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Philippe Rocca-Serra";
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://mathworld.wolfram.com/Cosine.html"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "cosine transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200169.
obi:0200018 iao:0000111 "loess group transformation one-channel"@en;
            iao:0000112 "A loess group transformation one-channel is a loess group transformation in the special case where the input is the result of an MA transformation applied to intensities from two related one-channel assays."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A loess group transformation one-channel is a loess group transformation in the special case where the input is the result of an MA transformation applied to intensities from two related one-channel assays."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OTHER: Editor's generalization based on MGED Ontology term"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "loess group transformation one-channel"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200024.
obi:0200019 iao:0000111 "loess group transformation two-channel"@en;
            iao:0000112 "A loess group transformation two-channel is a loess group transformation in the special case where the input is the result of an MA transformation applied to intensities from the two channels of a two-channel assay."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A loess group transformation two-channel is a loess group transformation in the special case where the input is the result of an MA transformation applied to intensities from the two channels of a two-channel assay."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OTHER: Editor's generalization based on MGED Ontology term"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "loess group transformation two-channel"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200024.
obi:0200020 iao:0000111 "homogeneous polynomial transformation"@en;
            iao:0000112 "a*x, with a non-zero, is a homogeneous polynomial of degree 1 in 1 variable, a*x^2, with a non-zero, is a homogeneous polynomial of degree 2 in 1 variable; a_1*x_1+...+a_n*x_n, with at least one of the a_i's non-zero, is a homogeneous polynomial of degree one in n variables; a*x_n^3+b*x_1*x_2*x_3, with at least one of a and b non-zero, is a homogeneous polynomial of degree 3 in n variables."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A homogeneous polynomial transformation is a polynomial transformation where all the term of the polynomial have the same degree."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://mathworld.wolfram.com/HomogeneousPolynomial.html"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "homogeneous polynomial transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200093.
obi:0200021 iao:0000111 "linlog transformation"@en;
            iao:0000112 "This can be used for microarray normalization, e.g. to normalize the data from a two-channel expression microarray assay, as described in PMID 16646782."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A linlog transformation is a data transformation, described in PMID 16646782, whose input is a matrix [y_ik] and whose output is a matrix obtained by applying formula (9) of this paper, where values below an appropriately determined threshold (dependent on the row i) are transformed via a polynomial of degree 1, and values above this threshold are transformed via a logarithm."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra",
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PMID: 16646782"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "linlog transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200169,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200022 iao:0000111 "variance stabilizing transformation"@en;
            iao:0000112 """This can be used for expression microarray assay normalization and it is referred to as \"variance stabilizing normalization\", according to the procedure described e.g. in PMID 12169536."""@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A variance stabilizing transformation is a data transformation, described in PMID 12169536, whose input is a matrix [y_ik] and whose output is a matrix obtained by applying formula (6) in this paper. One of the goals is to obtain an output matrix whose rows have equal variances. The method relies on various assumptions described in the paper."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en,
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000118 "variance stabilising transformation"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PMID: 12169536"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "variance stabilizing transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200169.
obi:0200023 iao:0000111 "loess global transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A loess global transformation is a loess transformation where only one loess fitting is performed, utilizing one subset of (or possibly all of) the data points in the input so that there is only one resulting loess curve y=f(x) which is used for the transformation."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en,
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "Philippe Rocca-Serra",
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OTHER: Editor's generalization based on MGED Ontology term"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "loess global transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200071.
obi:0200024 iao:0000111 "loess group transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A loess group transformation is a loess transformation where the input is partitioned into groups and for each group a loess fitting is performed, utilizing a subset of (or possibly all of) the data points in that group. Thus, a collection of loess curves y=f_i(x) is generated, one per group. Each (x, y) in the input is transformed into (x, y-f_i(x)), where f_i(x) is the curve corresponding to the group to which that data point belongs."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "James Malone"@en,
                        "Philippe Rocca-Serra";
            iao:0000119 "OTHER: Editor's generalization based on MGED Ontology term"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "loess group transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200071.
obi:0200025 iao:0000111 "loess scale group transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A loess scale group transformation is a data transformation consisting in the application of a scale adjustment following a loess group transformation, to render the group variances for the second variable (y) similar.  Has objective scaling."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "James Malone"@en,
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OTHER: Editor's generalization based on MGED Ontology term"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "loess scale group transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200183 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200024 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0002087 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200185.
obi:0200026 iao:0000111 "total intensity transformation single"@en;
            iao:0000112 "This can be used as a simple normalization method for expression microarray assays. For example, each intensity from a one-channel microarray assay is multiplied by a constant so that the output mean intensity over the microarray equals a desired target T (the multiplicative constant in this case is the T/(mean intensity))."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A total intensity transformation single is a data transformation that takes as input an n-dimensional (real) vector and multiplies each component of this vector by a coefficient, where the coefficient is obtained by taking the sum of the input components or of a subset of these, multiplied by a constant of choice."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra",
                        "Helen Parkinson"@en,
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "James Malone"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OTHER: Adjusted from MGED Ontology"@en;
            iao:0000232 """Note that if the word \"sum\" is replaced by the word \"mean\" in the definition, the resulting definition is equivalent."""@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "total intensity transformation single"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200169,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200027 iao:0000111 "total intensity transformation paired"@en;
            iao:0000112 "This can be used as a simple normalization method for the two channels from a two-channel expression microarray assay or from two related one-channel expression microarray assays."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A total intensity transformation paired is a data transformation that takes as input two n-dimensional (real) vectors and multiplies each component of the first vector by a coefficient, where the coefficient is obtained by taking the ratio of the sum of the second input components or of a subset of these by the sum of the first input components or of a subset of these (the same subset is used for the two vectors)."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Philippe Rocca-Serra";
            iao:0000119 "OTHER: Adjusted from MGED Ontology"@en;
            iao:0000232 """Note that if the word \"sum\" is replaced by the word \"mean\" in the definition, the resulting definition is equivalent."""@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "total intensity transformation paired"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200169,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200028 iao:0000111 "quantile transformation"@en;
            iao:0000112 """This can be used for expression microarray assay normalization and it is referred to as \"quantile normalization\", according to the procedure described e.g. in PMID 12538238."""@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A quantile transformation is a data transformation that takes as input a collection of data sets, where each can be thought as an n-dimensional (real) vector, and which transforms each data set so that the resulting output data sets have equal quantiles."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "quantile transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200169,
                            [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000674 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200177 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class],
                            obi:0200181.
obi:0200029 iao:0000111 "mean centering"@en;
            iao:0000112 "This can be used as a normalization method in expression microarray assays. For example, given a two-channel microarray assay, the log ratios of the two channels (M values) can be mean-centered."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A mean centering is a data transformation that takes as input an n-dimensional (real) vector, performs a mean calculation on its components, and subtracts the resulting mean from each component of the input."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra",
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000118 "mean centring"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "mean centering"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200169.
obi:0200030 iao:0000111 "median centering"@en;
            iao:0000112 "This can be used as a normalization method in expression microarray assays. For example, given a two-channel microarray assay, the log ratios of the two channels (M values) can be median-centered."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A median centering is a data transformation that takes as input an n-dimensional (real) vector, performs a median calculation on its components, and subtracts the resulting median from each component of the input."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra",
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000118 "median centring"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "median centering"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200169,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200031 iao:0000111 "differential expression analysis objective"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Analyses implemented by the SAM (http://www-stat.stanford.edu/~tibs/SAM), PaGE (www.cbil.upenn.edu/PaGE) or GSEA (www.broad.mit.edu/gsea/) algorithms and software"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A differential expression analysis objective is a data transformation objective whose input consists of expression levels of entities (such as transcripts or proteins), or of sets of such expression levels, under two or more conditions and whose output reflects which of these are likely to have different expression across such conditions."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "differential expression analysis objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200032 iao:0000111 "K-fold cross validation method"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "K-fold cross-validation randomly partitions the original sample into K subsamples. Of the K subsamples, a single subsample is retained as the validation data for testing the model, and the remaining K - 1 subsamples are used as training data. The cross-validation process is then repeated K times (the folds), with each of the K subsamples used exactly once as the validation data. The K results from the folds then can be averaged (or otherwise combined) to produce a single estimation. The advantage of this method over repeated random sub-sampling is that all observations are used for both training and validation, and each observation is used for validation exactly once. 10-fold cross-validation is commonly used";
            iao:0000117 "Person:Helen Parkinson";
            iao:0000119 "Tina Boussard";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "K-fold cross validation method"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200188 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000792.
obi:0200033 iao:0000111 "leave one out cross validation method"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The authors conducted  leave-one-out cross validation to estimate the strength and accuracy of the differentially expressed filtered genes. http://bioinformatics.oxfordjournals.org/cgi/content/abstract/19/3/368";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "is a data transformation :  leave-one-out cross-validation (LOOCV) involves using a single observation from the original sample as the validation data, and the remaining observations as the training data. This is repeated such that each observation in the sample is used once as the validation data";
            iao:0000116 "2009-11-10. Tracker: https://sourceforge.net/tracker/?func=detail&aid=2893049&group_id=177891&atid=886178";
            iao:0000117 "Person:Helen Parkinson";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "leave one out cross validation method"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000792,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200188 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200034 iao:0000111 "jackknifing method";
            iao:0000112 "simple weighting procedure is suggested for combining information over alleles and loci, and sample variances may be estimated by a jackknife procedure";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "Jacknifing is a re-sampling data transformation process used to estimate the precision of sampling statistics and is a resampling method";
            iao:0000117 "Helen Parkinson";
            iao:0000118 "jackknifing"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Resampling_%28statistics%29";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "jackknifing method"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000792,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200188 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200035 iao:0000111 "boostrapping"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Although widely accepted that high throughput biological data are typically highly noisy, the effects that this uncertainty has upon the conclusions we draw from these data are often overlooked. However, in order to assign any degree of confidence to our conclusions, we must quantify these effects. Bootstrap resampling is one method by which this may be achieved.";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "Bootstrapping is a statistical method for estimating the sampling distribution of a statistic by sampling with replacement from the original data, most often with the purpose of deriving robust estimates of standard errors and confidence intervals of a population parameter like a mean, median, proportion, odds ratio, correlation coefficient or regression coefficient"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Helen Parkinson";
            iao:0000119 "Bootstrapping is a data transformation process which estimates the precision of sampling statistics by drawing randomly with replacement from a set of data points";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "boostrapping"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000792,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200188 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200036 iao:0000111 "Benjamini and Hochberg false discovery rate correction method"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Statistical significance of the 8 most represented biological processes (GO level 4) among E7 6 month upregulated genes following analysis with DAVID software; Benjamini-Hochberg FDR (false discovery rate)";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A data transformation process in which the Benjamini and Hochberg method sequential p-value procedure  is applied with the aim of correcting false discovery rate";
            iao:0000116 """2011-03-31: [PRS]. 
specified input and output of dt which were missing"""@en;
            iao:0000117 "Helen Parkinson",
                        "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en;
            iao:0000119 "Helen Parkinson";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Benjamini and Hochberg false discovery rate correction method"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000175 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0001442 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000791 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200163,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000662 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200037 iao:0000111 "pareto scaling"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A pareto scaling is a data transformation that divides all measurements of a variable by the square root of the standard deviation of that variable."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PMID:16762068"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "pareto scaling"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200169,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200040 iao:0000111 "modular decomposition"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "Molecular decomposition is the partition of a network into distinct subgraphs for the purpose of identifying functional clusters. The network data is run through any of several existing algorithms designed to partition a network into distinct subgraphs for the purpose of isolating groups of functionally linked biological elements such as proteins."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en;
            iao:0000119 "editor"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "modular decomposition"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200080.
obi:0200041 iao:0000111 "k-means clustering"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A k-means clustering is a data transformation which achieves a class discovery or partitioning objective, which takes as input a collection of objects (represented as points in multidimensional space) and which partitions them into a specified number k of clusters. The algorithm attempts to find the centers of natural clusters in the data. The most common form of the algorithm starts by partitioning the input points into k initial sets, either at random or using some heuristic data. It then calculates the mean point, or centroid, of each set. It constructs a new partition by associating each point with the closest centroid. Then the centroids are recalculated for the new clusters, and the algorithm repeated by alternate applications of these two steps until convergence, which is obtained when the points no longer switch clusters (or alternatively centroids are no longer changed)."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi",
                        "Philippe Rocca-Serra",
                        "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K-means"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "k-means clustering"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200171,
                            [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000648 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200178 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200172 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200175.
obi:0200042 iao:0000111 "hierarchical clustering"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A hierarchical clustering is a data transformation which achieves a class discovery objective, which takes as input data item and builds a hierarchy of clusters. The traditional representation of this hierarchy is a tree (visualized by a dendrogram), with the individual input objects at one end (leaves) and a single cluster containing every object at the other (root)."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_clustering#Hierarchical_clustering"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "hierarchical clustering"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000648 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200178 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class],
                            obi:0200175.
obi:0200043 iao:0000111 "average linkage hierarchical clustering"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "An average linkage hierarchical clustering is an agglomerative hierarchical clustering which generates successive clusters based on a distance measure, where the distance between two clusters is calculated as the average distance between objects from the first cluster and objects from the second cluster."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "average linkage hierarchical clustering"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200154.
obi:0200044 iao:0000111 "complete linkage hierarchical clustering"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "an agglomerative hierarchical clustering which generates successive clusters based on a distance measure, where the distance between two clusters is calculated as the maximum distance between objects from the first cluster and objects from the second cluster."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "complete linkage hierarchical clustering"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200154.
obi:0200045 iao:0000111 "single linkage hierarchical clustering"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A single linkage hierarchical clustering is an agglomerative hierarchical clustering which generates successive clusters based on a distance measure, where the distance between two clusters is calculated as the minimum distance between objects from the first cluster and objects from the second cluster."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "single linkage hierarchical clustering"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200154.
obi:0200049 iao:0000111 "Benjamini and Yekutieli false discovery rate correction method"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The expression set was compared univariately between the stroke patients and controls, gene list was generated using False Discovery Rate correction (Benjamini and Yekutieli)";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A data transformation in which the Benjamini and Yekutieli method is applied with the aim of correcting false discovery rate";
            iao:0000116 """2011-03-31: [PRS]. 
specified input and output of dt which were missing"""@en;
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en,
                        "Helen Parkinson";
            iao:0000119 "Helen Parkinson";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Benjamini and Yekutieli false discovery rate correction method"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200163,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000175 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0001442 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000791 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000662 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200050 iao:0000111 "dimensionality reduction"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A dimensionality reduction is data partitioning which transforms each input m-dimensional vector (x_1, x_2, ..., x_m) into an output n-dimensional vector (y_1, y_2, ..., y_n), where n is smaller than m."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra",
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000118 "data projection";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "dimensionality reduction"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000648 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200178 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class],
                            obi:0200175.
obi:0200051 iao:0000111 "principal components analysis dimensionality reduction"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A principal components analysis dimensionality reduction is a dimensionality reduction achieved by applying principal components analysis and by keeping low-order principal components and excluding higher-order ones."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Philippe Rocca-Serra",
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en;
            iao:0000118 "pca data reduction"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "principal components analysis dimensionality reduction"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200050.
obi:0200052 iao:0000111 "probabilistic algorithm"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A probabilistic algorithm is one which involves an element of probability or randomness in the transformation of the data."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "probabilistic algorithm"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000.
obi:0200053 iao:0000111 "expectation maximization"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "EM is a probabilistic algorithm used to estimate the maximum likelihood of parameters from existing data where the model involves unobserved latent variables. The input to this method is the data model for which the estimation is performed over and the output is an approximated probability function."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "expectation maximization"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200052.
obi:0200054 iao:0000111 "global modularity calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A network graph quality calculation in which an input data set of subgraph modules and their in-degree and out-degree qualities is used to calculate the average modularity of subgraphs within the network."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "global modularity calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200147.
obi:0200055 iao:0000111 "dye swap merge"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A dye swap merge is a replicate analysis which takes as input data from paired two-channel microarray assays where the sample labeled with one dye in the first assay is labeled with the other dye in the second assay and vice versa. The output for each reporter is obtained by combining its (raw or possibly pre-processed) M values in the two assays, where the M value in an assay is defined as the difference of the log intensities in the two channels. This can be used as a normalization step, when appropriate assumptions are met."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone"@en,
                        "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "dye swap merge"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200057.
obi:0200056 iao:0000111 "moving average"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The moving average is often used to handle data from tiling arrays."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A moving average is a data transformation in which center calculations, usually mean calculations, are performed on values within a sliding window across the input data set."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Helen Parkinson"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Philippe Rocca-Serra";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "PERSON: Helen Parkinson"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "moving average"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000679 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000425 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class],
                            obi:0200170.
obi:0200057 iao:0000111 "replicate analysis"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Replicate analysis can be used in microarray analysis to identify and potentially exclude low quality data."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A replicate analysis is a data transformation in which data from replicates are combined, e.g. through descriptive statistics calculations, and the results might be utilized for a variety of purposes, like assessing reproducibility, identifying outliers, normalizing, etc."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Helen Parkinson"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON:Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "PERSON: Helen Parkinson"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "replicate analysis"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200169,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200058 iao:0000111 "b cell epitope prediction"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A B cell epitope prediction takes as input an antigen sequence, and through an analysis of this sequence, produces as output a prediction of the likelihood the biomaterial is a B Cell Epitope."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Helen Parkinson"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Helen Parkinson"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "b cell epitope prediction"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200081 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200187.
obi:0200059 iao:0000111 "mhc binding prediction"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "An MHC binding prediction takes an input of a biomaterial sequence and through an analysis of this sequence, produces as output a prediction of the likelihood that the biomaterial will bind to an MHC molecule."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Helen Parkinson"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Helen Parkinson"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "mhc binding prediction"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200081 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200187.
obi:0200060 iao:0000111 "t cell epitope prediction"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A T cell epitope prediction takes as input an antigen sequence, and through an analysis of this sequence, produces as output a prediction of the likelihood the biomaterial is a T cell epitope."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Helen Parkinson"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Helen Parkinson"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "t cell epitope prediction"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200081 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200187.
obi:0200061 iao:0000111 "data imputation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "Imputation is a means of filling in missing data values from a predictive distribution of the missing values.  The predictive distribution can be created either based on a formal statistical model (i,e, a multivariate normal distribution) or an algorithm."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee"@en;
            iao:0000119 "ARTICLE: Little, RJA and Rubin, DB (2002).  Statistical Analysis with Missing Data, Second Edition.  John Wiley: Hoboken New Jersey, pp. 59-60."@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "data imputation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000.
obi:0200062 iao:0000111 "continuum mass spectrum"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A continuum mass spectrum is a data transformation that contains the full profile of the detected signals for a given ion."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en,
                        "PERSON: James Malone";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Tina Boussard"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "continuum mass spectrum"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200197 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200085.
obi:0200063 iao:0000111 "characteristic path length calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "Quantifying subgraph navigability based on shortest-path length averaged over all pairs of subgraph vertices"@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "characteristic path length calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200197 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200085.
obi:0200064 iao:0000111 "centroid mass spectrum"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A centroid mass spectrum is a data transformation in which many points are used to delineate a mass spectral peak, is converted into mass-centroided data by a data compression algorithm. The centroided mass peak is located at the weighted center of mass of the profile peak. The normalized area of the peak provides the mass intensity data."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Person:Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en;
            iao:0000118 "centroid mass spectrum calculation",
                        "centroiding";
            iao:0000119 "centroid mass spectrum"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "centroid mass spectrum"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200085,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200197 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200066 iao:0000111 "Holm-Bonferroni family-wise error rate correction method"@en;
            iao:0000112 "t-tests were used with the type I error adjusted for multiple comparisons, Holm's correction (HOLM 1979), and false discovery rate, http://www.genetics.org/cgi/content/full/172/2/1179";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "a data transformation that performs more than one hypothesis test simultaneously, a closed-test procedure, that  controls the familywise error rate for all the k hypotheses at level α in the strong sense. Objective: multiple testing correction";
            iao:0000116 """2011-03-14: [PRS]. Class Label has been changed to address the conflict with the definition
Also added restriction to specify the output to be a FWER adjusted p-value

The 'editor preferred term' should be removed"""@en;
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en,
                        "Person:Helen Parkinson";
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holm%E2%80%93Bonferroni_method";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Holm-Bonferroni family-wise error rate correction method"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000791 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000175 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200073,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0001265 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200070 iao:0000111 "edge weighting"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "Edge weighting is the substitution or transformation of edge length using numerical data.  Data input include a symmetric adjacency matrix for a network and a second data set, for example a list of interactor pairs and a confidence score associated with the experimental detection of each pair's interaction.  Each element in the adjacency matrix is transformed or replaced with the corresponding number in the second data set.  Output data are a modified adjacency matrix reflecting the transformed state of the network."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en;
            iao:0000119 "editor"@en;
            iao:0000232 """was classified under algorithm class which is not acceptable super-class
TO BE DEALT WITH STILL BY RICHARD.  JAMES"""@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "edge weighting"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200080.
obi:0200071 iao:0000111 "loess transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A loess transformation is a data transformation that takes as input a collection of real number pairs (x, y) and, after performing (one or more) loess fittings, utilizes the resulting curves to transform each (x, y) in the input into (x, y-f(x)) where f(x) is one of the fitted curves."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "James Malone"@en,
                        "Philippe Rocca-Serra";
            iao:0000119 "OTHER: Editor's generalization based on MGED Ontology term"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "loess transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200169,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200072 iao:0000111 "curve fitting data transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A curve fitting is a data transformation that has objective curve fitting and that consists of finding a curve which matches a series of data points and possibly other constraints."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curve_fitting"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "curve fitting data transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:unionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000656 ; 
                                              owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                              a owl:Restriction]
                                              [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200174 ; 
                                              owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                              a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                 a owl:Class].
obi:0200073 iao:0000111 "family wise error rate correction method"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A family wise error rate correction method is a multiple testing procedure that controls the probability of at least one false positive.";
            iao:0000116 """2011-03-31: [PRS]. 
creating a defined class by specifying the necessary output of dt
allows correct classification of FWER dt"""@en;
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en,
                        "Monnie McGee";
            iao:0000118 "FWER correction"@en;
            iao:0000119 "Dudoit, Sandrine and van der Laan, Mark J. (2008) Multiple Testing Procedures with Applications to Genomics.  New York: Springer , p. 19";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "family wise error rate correction method"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000791 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200089;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0001265 ; 
                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                 a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200074 iao:0000111 "submatrix extraction"@en;
            iao:0000112 "When presented with the data from an expression microarray experiment in the form of a matrix, whose rows correspond to genes and whose columns correspond to samples, if one filters some of the genes and/or some of the samples out, the resulting data set corresponds to a submatrix of the original set."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A submatrix extraction is a projection whose input is a matrix and whose output is a matrix obtained by selecting certain rows and columns from the input. (Note that, if one represents the input matrix as a vector obtained by concatenating its rows, then extracting a submatrix is equivalent to projecting this vector into that composed by the entries belonging to the rows and columns of interest from the input matrix.)"@en;
            iao:0000116 "Note that this can be considered as a special case of projection if one represents the input matrix as a vector obtained by concatenating its rows. Then extracting a submatrix is equivalent to projecting this vector into the entries belonging to the rows and columns of interest from the input matrix."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en,
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Submatrix"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "submatrix extraction"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200050.
obi:0200075 iao:0000111 "row submatrix extraction"@en;
            iao:0000112 "When presented with the data from an expression microarray experiment in the form of a matrix, whose rows correspond to genes and whose columns correspond to samples, if one filters some of the genes out, the resulting data set corresponds to a row submatrix of the original set."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A row submatrix extraction is a submatrix extraction where all the columns of the input matrix are retained and selection only occurs on the rows."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "James Malone"@en,
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "row submatrix extraction"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200074.
obi:0200076 iao:0000111 "column submatrix extraction"@en;
            iao:0000112 "When presented with the data from an expression microarray experiment in the form of a matrix, whose rows correspond to genes and whose columns correspond to samples, if one filters some of the samples out, the resulting data set corresponds to a column submatrix of the original set."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A column submatrix extraction is a submatrix extraction where all the rows of the input matrix are retained and selection only occurs on the columns."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "column submatrix extraction"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200074.
obi:0200077 iao:0000111 "gating"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "Gating is a property-based vector selection with the objective of partitioning a data vector set into vector subsets based on dimension values of individual vectors (events), in which vectors represent individual physical particles (often cells) of a sample and dimension values represent light intensity qualities as measured by flow cytometry."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Josef Spidlen"@en,
                        "Richard Scheuermann"@en,
                        "Ryan Brinkman"@en,
                        "James Malone"@en,
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en,
                        "PERSON: Josef Spidlen"@en,
                        "PERSON: James Malone"@en,
                        "PERSON:Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "PERSON: Ryan Brinkman"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "gating"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200172 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200157 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200182,
                            obi:0200171.
obi:0200078 iao:0000111 "descriptive statistical calculation objective"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A descriptive statistical calculation objective is a data transformation objective which concerns any calculation intended to describe a feature of a data set, for example, its center or its variability."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Monnie McGee"@en,
                        "James Malone"@en,
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "PERSON: Monnie McGee"@en,
                        "PERSON: James Malone"@en,
                        "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "descriptive statistical calculation objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200079 iao:0000111 "arithmetic mean calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "An arithmetic mean calculation is a descriptive statistics calculation in which the mean is calculated by taking the sum of all of the observations in a data set divided by the total number of observations. It gives a measure of the 'center of gravity' for the data set. It is also known as the first moment."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee"@en,
                        "Philippe Rocca-Serra",
                        "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone"@en,
                        "PERSON: Monnie McGee"@en;
            iao:0000232 "From Monnie's file comments - need to add moment_calculation and center_calculation roles but they don't exist yet - (editor note added by James Jan 2008)"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "arithmetic mean calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200078 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000674 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200177 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class],
                            obi:0200184,
                            obi:0200170,
                            [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000679 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000425 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class],
                            obi:0200181.
obi:0200080 iao:0000111 "network analysis"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A data transformation that takes as input data that describes biological networks in terms of the node (a.k.a. vertex) and edge graph elements and their characteristics and generates as output properties of the constituent nodes and edges, the sub-graphs, and the entire network."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000118 "network topology analysis";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "network analysis"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000.
obi:0200081 iao:0000111 "sequence analysis objective"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A sequence analysis objective is a data transformation objective which aims to analyse some ordered biological data for sequential patterns."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "sequence analysis objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200082 iao:0000111 "longitudinal data analysis";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "Longitudinal analysis is a data transformation used to perform repeated observations of the same items over long periods of time."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Tina Boussard",
                        "PERSON: James Malone";
            iao:0000118 "longitudinal data analysis"@en,
                        "correlation analysis";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "longitudinal data analysis"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200196 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200083 iao:0000111 "survival analysis objective"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Kaplan meier data transformation";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A data transformation objective which has the data transformation aims to model time to event data (where events are e.g. death and or disease recurrence); the purpose of survival analysis is to model the underlying distribution of event times and to assess the dependence of the event time on other explanatory variables";
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Tina Boussard",
                        "PERSON: James Malone";
            iao:0000118 "survival analysis";
            iao:0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Survival_analysis";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "survival analysis objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200085 iao:0000111 "mass spectrometry analysis"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A data transformation which has the objective of spectrum analysis.";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "mass spectrometry analysis"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200197 ; 
                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                 a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200086 iao:0000111 "spread calculation data transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A spread calculation is a data transformation that has objective spread calculation."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "EDITOR";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "spread calculation data transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200180 ; 
                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                 a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200088 iao:0000111 "Kaplan Meier"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "a nonparametric (actuarial) data transformation technique for estimating time-related events. It is a univariate analysis that estimates the probability of the proportion of subjects in remission at a particular time, starting from the initiation of active date (time zero), and takes into account those lost to follow-up or not yet in remission at end of study (censored)";
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: James Malone",
                        "PERSON: Tina Boussard";
            iao:0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaplan%E2%80%93Meier_estimator";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Kaplan Meier"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200083 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200194.
obi:0200089 iao:0000111 "multiple testing correction method";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A multiple testing correction method is a hypothesis test performed simultaneously on M > 1 hypotheses.  Multiple testing procedures produce a set of rejected hypotheses that is an estimate for the set of false null hypotheses while controlling for a suitably define Type I error rate";
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee";
            iao:0000118 "multiple testing procedure"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PAPER: Dudoit, Sandrine and van der Laan, Mark J. (2008) Multiple Testing Procedures with Applications to Genomics.  New York: Springer , p. 9-10.";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "multiple testing correction method"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000668;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000791 ; 
                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                 a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200091 iao:0000111 "inter-rater reliability objective";
            iao:0000112 """A study was conducted to determine the inter-rater reliability of common clinical examination procedures proposed to identify patients with lumbar segmental instability.

Examples include joint-probability of agreement, Cohen's kappa and the related Fleiss' kappa, inter-rater correlation, concordance correlation coefficient and intra-class correlation.""";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "a data transformation objective of determining the concordance or agreement between human judges.";
            iao:0000117 "Person:Helen Parkinson",
                        "Person:Alan Ruttenberg";
            iao:0000118 "inter-rater agreement";
            iao:0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inter-rater_reliability";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "inter-rater reliability objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200092 iao:0000111 "Westfall and Young family wise error rate correction"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "Is a data transformation process in which the Westfall and Young method is applied with the aim of controlling for multiple testing";
            iao:0000116 "PRS: 2011-03-31: set specified input and specified output to the data transformation"@en,
                        """2011-03-31: [PRS]. 
specified input and output of dt which were missing"""@en;
            iao:0000117 "Helen Parkinson";
            iao:0000118 "Westfall and Young FWER correction"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Westfall and Young family wise error rate correction"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000791 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0001265 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000175 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200073.
obi:0200093 iao:0000111 "polynomial transformation"@en;
            iao:0000112 """a*x+b, with a non-zero, is a polynomial of degree one in one variable;  a*x^2+b*x+c, with a nonzero, is a polynomial of degree 2 in 1
variable; a*x*y+b*y+c, with a non-zero, is a polynomial of degree 2 in 2 variables (x and y); a_1*x_1+...+a_n*x_n+b, with at least one of the a_i's non-zero, is a polynomial of degree one in n variables"""@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A polynomial transformation is a data transformation that is obtained through a polynomial, where a polynomial is a mathematical expression involving a sum of powers in one or more variables multiplied by coefficients (e.g. see http://mathworld.wolfram.com/Polynomial.html). The number of variables and the degree are properties of a polynomial. The degree of a polynomial is the highest power of its terms, where the terms of a polynomial are the individual summands with the coefficients omitted."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://mathworld.wolfram.com/Polynomial.html"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "polynomial transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000.
obi:0200094 iao:0000111 "logarithmic transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A logarithmic transformation is a data transformation consisting in the application of the logarithm function with a given base a (where a>0 and a is not equal to 1) to a (one dimensional) positive real number input. The logarithm function with base a can be defined as the inverse of the exponential function with the same base. See e.g. http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logarithm."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logarithm"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "logarithmic transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200169.
obi:0200095 iao:0000111 "exponential transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An exponential transformation is a data transformation consisting in the application of the exponential function with a given base a (where a>0 and a is typically not equal to 1) to a (one dimensional) real number input. For alternative definitions and properties of this function see, e.g., http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exponential_function and http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Characterizations_of_the_exponential_function."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Characterizations_of_the_exponential_function"@en,
                        "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exponential_function"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "exponential transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200169.
obi:0200097 iao:0000111 "non-negative matrix factorization";
            iao:0000112 "Non-negative matrix factorization is used in text mining where document-term matrix is constructed with the weights of various terms (typically weighted word frequency information) from a set of documents. This matrix is factored into a term-feature and a feature-document matrix.";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "Non negative matrix factorization is a data transformation in which factorises a matrix and which forces that all elements must be equal to or greater than zero.";
            iao:0000119 "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-negative_matrix_factorization";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "non-negative matrix factorization"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000.
obi:0200098 iao:0000111 "soft independent modeling of class analogy analysis";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "Soft independent modeling by class analogy (SIMCA) is a descriptive statistics method for supervised classification of data. The method requires a training data set consisting of samples (or objects) with a set of attributes and their class membership. The term soft refers to the fact the classifier can identify samples as belonging to multiple classes and not necessarily producing a classification of samples into non-overlapping classes."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en;
            iao:0000118 "SIMCA"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soft_independent_modelling_of_class_analogies"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "soft independent modeling of class analogy analysis"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200169,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200099 iao:0000111 "discriminant function analysis"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "Discriminant function analysis is a form of discriminant analysis used to determine which variables discriminate between two or more naturally occurring groups. Analysis is used to determine which variable(s) are the best predictors of a particular outcome."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://www.statsoft.com/textbook/stdiscan.html"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "discriminant function analysis"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200106,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000648 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000023 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200179 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class],
                            obi:0200175,
                            obi:0000663.
obi:0200100 iao:0000111 "canonical variate analysis"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "canonical variate analysis is a form of discriminant analysis that takes several continuous predictor variables and uses the entire set to predict several criterion variables, each of which is also continuous. CVA simultaneously calculates a linear composite of all x variables and  a linear composite of all y variables. Unlike other multivariate techniques, these weighted composites are derived in pairs. Each linear combination is called a canonical variate and takes the general linear form."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en;
            iao:0000118 "CVA"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canonical_analysis"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "canonical variate analysis"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200171,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200172 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200106.
obi:0200101 iao:0000111 "linear discriminant functional analysis"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "Linear discriminant functional analysis (LDFA) is a multivariate technique used in special applications where there are several intact groups (random assignment may be impossible) and they have been measured on several independent measures. Thus, you will want to describe how these groups differ on the basis of these measures. In this case, classification and prediction is the main objective."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "linear discriminant functional analysis"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000663,
                            obi:0200106,
                            [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000023 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200179 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000648 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200175.
obi:0200102 iao:0000111 "regression analysis method"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "Regression analysis is a descriptive statistics technique that examines the relation of a dependent variable (response variable) to specified independent variables (explanatory variables). Regression analysis can be used as a descriptive method of data analysis (such as curve fitting) without relying on any assumptions about underlying processes generating the data."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en;
            iao:0000119 "BOOK: Richard A. Berk, Regression Analysis: A Constructive Critique, Sage Publications (2004) 978-0761929048"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "regression analysis method"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000.
obi:0200103 iao:0000111 "multiple linear regression analysis"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 """multiple linear regression is a regression method that models the relationship between a dependent variable Y, independent variables Xi, i = 1, ..., p, and a random term epsilon. The model can be written as
    Y = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 X_1 + \\beta_2 X_2 + \\cdots +\\beta_p X_p + \\varepsilon
where \\beta_0 =  0 is the intercept (\"constant\" term), the \\beta_i s  are the respective parameters of independent variables, and p is the number of parameters to be estimated in the linear regression."""@en;
            iao:0000117 "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB:http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linear_regression"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "multiple linear regression analysis"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200102.
obi:0200104 iao:0000111 "principal component regression"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "The Principal Component Regression method is a regression analysis method that combines the Principal Component Analysis (PCA)spectral decomposition with an Inverse Least Squares (ILS) regression method to create a quantitative model for complex samples. Unlike quantitation methods based directly on Beer's Law which attempt to calculate the absorbtivity coefficients for the constituents of interest from a direct regression of the constituent concentrations onto the spectroscopic responses, the PCR method regresses the concentrations on the PCA scores."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: : http://www.thermo.com/com/cda/resources/resources_detail/1,2166,13414,00.html"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "principal component regression"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200175,
                            obi:0200102,
                            [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000648 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200178 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class].
obi:0200105 iao:0000111 "partial least square regression analysis"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 """Partial least squares regression is an extension of the multiple linear regression model (see, e.g., Multiple Regression or General Stepwise Regression). In its simplest form, a linear model specifies the (linear) relationship between a dependent (response) variable Y, and a set of predictor variables, the X's, so that
Y = b0 + b1X1 + b2X2 + ... + bpXp
In this equation b0 is the regression coefficient for the intercept and the bi values are the regression coefficients (for variables 1 through p) computed from the data."""@en;
            iao:0000117 "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en;
            iao:0000118 "PLS-RA"@en;
            iao:0000119 "ARTICLE: de Jong, S. (1993). SIMPLS: An alternative approach to partial least squares regression. Chemometrics and Intelligent Laboratory Systems, 18: 251-263."@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "partial least square regression analysis"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200102.
obi:0200106 iao:0000111 "discriminant analysis"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "Discriminant function analysis is used to determine which variables discriminate between two or more naturally occurring groups. Analysis is used to determine which variable(s) are the best predictors of a particular outcome."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Tina Hernandez-Boussard"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://www.statsoft.com/textbook/stdiscan.html"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "discriminant analysis"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000.
obi:0200107 iao:0000111 "partial least square discriminant analysis"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "PLS Discriminant Analysis (PLS-DA) is a discriminant analysis performed in order to sharpen the separation between groups of observations, by hopefully rotating PCA (Principal Components Analysis) components such that a maximum separation among classes is obtained, and to understand which variables carry the class separating information.";
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000118 "PLS-DA"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://www.camo.com/rt/Resources/pls-da.html";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "partial least square discriminant analysis"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200106.
obi:0200108 iao:0000111 "eh transformation"@en;
            iao:0000112 "This type of transformation is typically used in flow cytometry."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An eh transformation is a data transformation obtained by applying the function EH described in what follows to a (one dimensional) real number input. EH(x)=exp(x*d/r)+b*(d/r)*x-1, if x>=0, and EH(x)=-exp(-x*d/r)+b*(d/r)*x+1, otherwise. Here exp denotes an exponential transformation and b, d, r are positive real constants with the objective of normalization."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Joseph Spliden"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Ryan Brinkman"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://flowcyt.sourceforge.net/gating/latest.pdf"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "eh transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200169,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200109 iao:0000111 "b transformation"@en;
            iao:0000112 "This type of transformation is typically used in flow cytometry."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A b transformation is a data transformation obtained by applying the function B described in what follows to a (one dimensional) real number input. B(x)= a*exp(b*x)-c*exp(-d*x)+f, where exp denotes an exponential transformation and a, b, c, d, f are real constants with a, b, c, d positive with the objective of normalization."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Joseph Spliden"@en,
                        "Ryan Brinkman"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://flowcyt.sourceforge.net/gating/latest.pdf"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "b transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000451 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class],
                            obi:0200169.
obi:0200110 iao:0000111 "s transformation"@en;
            iao:0000112 "This type of transformation is typically used in flow cytometry."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An s transformation is a data transformation obtained by applying the function S described in what follows to a (one dimensional) real number input. S(x)=T*exp(w-m)*(exp(x-w)-(p^2)*exp((w-x)/p)+p^2-1) if x>=w, S(x)=-S(w-x) otherwise; where exp denotes an exponential_transformations, 'p^' denotes the exponential transformation with base p; T, w, m, p are real constants with T, m, and p positive and w non-negative, and where w and p are related by w=2p*ln(p)(p+1) with the objective of normalization."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Ryan Brinkman"@en,
                        "Joseph Spliden"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://flowcyt.sourceforge.net/gating/latest.pdf"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "s transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200169,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200111 iao:0000111 "data visualization";
            iao:0000112 "Generation of a heatmap from a microarray dataset";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An planned process that creates images, diagrams or animations from the input data."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en,
                        "Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "Tina Boussard"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000118 "visualization"@en,
                        "data encoding as image";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en,
                        "PERSON: James Malone"@en,
                        "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "PERSON: Tina Boussard"@en;
            iao:0000232 """Possible future hierarchy might include this:
information_encoding
>data_encoding
>>image_encoding""";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "data visualization"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000011,
                            [owl:allValuesFrom iao:0000027 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000027 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:allValuesFrom [owl:unionOf (iao:0000038
                                                             iao:0000101) ; 
                                                a owl:Class] ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom [owl:unionOf (iao:0000038
                                                              iao:0000101) ; 
                                                 a owl:Class] ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200113 iao:0000111 "similarity calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A similarity calculation is a data transformation that attaches to each pair of objects in the input a number that is meant to reflect how 'close' or 'similar' those objects are."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "similarity calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000023 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000648 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000663,
                            obi:0200175.
obi:0200114 iao:0000111 "euclidean distance calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An euclidean distance calculation is a similarity calculation that attaches to each pair of real number vectors of the same dimension n the square root of the sum of the square differences between corresponding components. The smaller this number, the more similar the two vectors are considered."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "euclidean distance calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200113.
obi:0200115 iao:0000111 "pearson correlation coefficient calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 """A pearson correlation coefficient calculation is a similarity calculation which attaches to each pair of random variables X and Y the ratio of their covariance by the product of their standard deviations. Given a series of n measurements of X and Y written as x_i and y_i where i = 1, 2, ..., n, then their Pearson correlation coefficient refers to the \"sample correlation coefficient\" and is written as the sum over i of the ratios (x_i-xbar)*(y_i-ybar)/((n-1)*s_x*s_y) where xbar and ybar are the sample means of X and Y , s_x and s_y are the sample standard deviations of X and Y. The closer the pearson correlation coefficient is to 1, the more similar the inputs are considered."""@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Correlation"@en,
                        "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "pearson correlation coefficient calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200113.
obi:0200116 iao:0000111 "loess fitting"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A loess fitting is a curve fitting obtained by localized regression. The latter refers to fitting a polynomial (straight line, quadratic, cubic, etc) to data values within a window covering a fraction of the total number of observations. As the window slides along the axis, a new polynomial is fit to the observations falling within the window. This continues until all points are fit with a local polynomial. The results are then smoothed together to form a curve. The smoothness of loess fits is controlled by a smoothing parameter (often denoted as alpha, usually between 1/4 and 1) and the degree of the polynomial that is fitted by the method (usually denoted by lambda)."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee"@en,
                        "Philippe Rocca-Serra";
            iao:0000119 "ARTICLE: Mathematical details of loess fits are given in Cleveland, William (1993) Visualizing Data. Hobart Press, Summit, New Jersey, pp. 94-101."@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "loess fitting"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200072,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200174 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200117 iao:0000111 "mode calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A mode calculation is a descriptive statistics calculation in which the mode is calculated which is the most common value in a data set. It is most often used as a measure of center for discrete data."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en,
                        "Monnie McGee"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Monnie McGee"@en,
                        "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000232 "From Monnie's file comments - need to add center_calculation role but it doesn't exist yet - (editor note added by James Jan 2008)"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "mode calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200181,
                            [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000674 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200177 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200078 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200184.
obi:0200118 iao:0000111 "quantile calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A quantile calculation is a descriptive statistics calculation in which the kth quantile is the data value for which an approximate k fraction of the data is less than or equal to that value.  See http://www.stat.wvu.edu/SRS/Modules/Quantiles/quantiles.html for details."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://www.stat.wvu.edu/SRS/Modules/Quantiles/quantiles.html"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "quantile calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200078 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200184.
obi:0200119 iao:0000111 "median calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A median calculation is a  descriptive statistics calculation in which the midpoint of the data set (the 0.5 quantile) is calculated.  First, the observations are sorted in increasing order.  For an odd number of observations, the median is the middle value of the sorted data.  For an even number of observations, the median is the average of the two middle values."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee"@en,
                        "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone"@en,
                        "PERSON: Monnie McGee"@en;
            iao:0000232 "From Monnie's file comments - need to add center_calculation role but it doesn't exist yet - (editor note added by James Jan 2008)"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "median calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000674 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200177 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class],
                            obi:0200184,
                            obi:0200181,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200078 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200120 iao:0000111 "variance calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A variance calculation is a descriptive statistics calculation in which the variance is defined as the average squared distance of each observation in the data set to the mean of the data set.  It is also known as the second central moment."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Monnie McGee"@en;
            iao:0000232 "From Monnie's file comments - need to add spread_calculation and moment_calculation roles but they don't exist yet - (editor note added by James Jan 2008)"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "variance calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200086,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200180 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200184,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200078 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200121 iao:0000111 "standard deviation calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A standard deviation calculation is a descriptive statistics calculation defined as the square root of the variance.  Also thought of as the average distance of each value to the mean."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Monnie McGee"@en;
            iao:0000232 "From Monnie's file comments - need to add spread calculation role but they doesn't exist yet - (editor note added by James Jan 2008)"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "standard deviation calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200078 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200086,
                            obi:0200184,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200180 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200122 iao:0000111 "interquartile-range calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The interquartile range is a descriptive statistics calculation defined as the difference between the 0.75 quantile and the 0.25 quantile for a set of data."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Monnie McGee"@en;
            iao:0000232 "From Monnie's file comments - need to add spread calculation role but they doesn't exist yet - (editor note added by James Jan 2008)"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "interquartile-range calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200078 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200086,
                            obi:0200184,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200180 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200123 iao:0000111 "skewness calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A skewness calculation is a descriptive statistics calculation defined as a parameter that describes how much a distribution (or a data set) varies from a bell-shaped curve.  See http://www.riskglossary.com/link/skewness.htm for details.  It is also known as the third central moment"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://www.riskglossary.com/link/skewness.htm"@en;
            iao:0000232 "From Monnie's file comments - need to add moment calculation role but they doesn't exist yet - (editor note added by James Jan 2008)"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "skewness calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200181,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200078 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200184,
                            [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000674 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200177 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class].
obi:0200124 iao:0000111 "kurtosis calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A kurtosis calculation is a descriptive statistics calculation defined as a parameter that measures how large or small the tails of a distribution are relative to the mean.  For details, see http://davidmlane.com/hyperstat/A53638.html"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://davidmlane.com/hyperstat/A53638.html"@en;
            iao:0000232 "From Monnie's file comments - need to add moment calculation role but they doesn't exist yet - (editor note added by James Jan 2008)"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "kurtosis calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200078 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200086,
                            obi:0200184,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200180 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200125 iao:0000111 "data combination"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A data transformation in which individual input data elements and values are merged together into a output set of data elements and values."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000118 "data pooling";
            iao:0000119 "editor"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "data combination"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200189 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200126 iao:0000111 "network graph construction"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A network analysis in which an input data set describing objects and relationships between objects is transformed into an output representation of these objects as nodes and the relationships as edges of a network graph."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "network graph construction"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200080.
obi:0200127 iao:0000111 "weighted network graph construction"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A network graph construction in which an input data set describing objects and quantitative relationships between objects is transformed into and output representation of these objects as nodes and the quantitative relationships as weighted edges of a network graph."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "weighted network graph construction"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200126.
obi:0200128 iao:0000111 "directed network graph construction"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A network graph construction in which an input data set describing objects and directional relationships between objects is transformed into and output representation of these objects as nodes and the directional relationships as directed edges of a network graph."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "directed network graph construction"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200126.
obi:0200129 iao:0000111 "node quality calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A network analysis in which an input data set describing node objects and edge relationships between node objects is used to determine the output quality of one of the node objects in the network."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "node quality calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200080.
obi:0200130 iao:0000111 "node degree calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A node quality calculation in which an input data set describing object nodes and relationship edges between object nodes is used to enumerate the number of unique relationships of an individual object node."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "node degree calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200129.
obi:0200131 iao:0000111 "quantitative node degree calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A node quality calculation in which an input data set describing object nodes and quantitative relationship edges between object nodes is used to sum all of the quantitative relationships of an individual object node."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "quantitative node degree calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200129.
obi:0200132 iao:0000111 "node in-degree calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A node quality calculation in which an input data set describing object nodes and directional relationship edges between object nodes is used to enumerate the number of unique relationships pointing into an individual object node."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "node in-degree calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200129.
obi:0200133 iao:0000111 "node out-degree calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A node quality calculation in which an input data set describing object nodes and directional relationship edges between object nodes is used to enumerate the number of unique relationships pointing out of an individual object node."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "node out-degree calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200129.
obi:0200134 iao:0000111 "node shortest path identification"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A node quality calculation in which a path describing the shortest path needed to transverse through connected nodes and edges to arrive at a specific target node in the network."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "node shortest path identification"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200129.
obi:0200135 iao:0000111 "edge quality calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A network analysis in which an input data set describing node objects and edge relationships between node objects is used to determine the output quality of one of the edge relationships in the network."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "edge quality calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200080.
obi:0200136 iao:0000111 "edge betweenness calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "An edge quality calculation in which the input is a data sets of shortest paths between all pairs of node in the network and the output is the sum of all shortest paths that traverse the specific edge."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "edge betweenness calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200135.
obi:0200137 iao:0000111 "network subgraph quality calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A network analysis in which an input data set describing node objects and edge relationships between node objects is used to determine the output quality of a subgraph partition of the network."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "network subgraph quality calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200080.
obi:0200138 iao:0000111 "subgraph degree calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A network subgraph quality calculation in which an input data set describing subgraphs and relationship edges between subgraphs and other network objects is used to enumerate the number of unique relationships of an individual subgraph."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "subgraph degree calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200137.
obi:0200139 iao:0000111 "quantitative subgraph degree calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A network subgraph quality calculation in which an input data set describing subgraphs and quantitative relationship edges between subgraphs and other network objects is used to sum the quantitative relationships of an individual subgraph."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "quantitative subgraph degree calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200137.
obi:0200140 iao:0000111 "mathematical feature";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "feature is a (parent_class) that describes a characteristic, trait or quality of a data transformation"@en;
            iao:0000116 "This class is temporary and will be placed outside of data transformation ultimately (if it still remains at all after review)"@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "mathematical feature"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000.
obi:0200141 iao:0000111 "log base";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The log base is a feature of a logarithmic function which is defined in http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logarithm. Its value can be any positive real number different from 1.";
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi";
            iao:0000118 "logarithm base",
                        "logarithmic base";
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logarithm";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "log base"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom xsd:float ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000292 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200140.
obi:0200143 iao:0000111 "subgraph in-degree calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A network subgraph quality calculation in which an input data set describing subgraphs and directional relationship edges between subgraphs and other network objects is used to enumerate the number of unique relationships pointing into an individual subgraph."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "subgraph in-degree calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200137.
obi:0200144 iao:0000111 "subgraph out-degree calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A network subgraph quality calculation in which an input data set describing subgraphs and relationship edges between subgraphs and other network objects is used to enumerate the number of unique relationships pointing out of an individual subgraph."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "subgraph out-degree calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200137.
obi:0200145 iao:0000111 "intra subgraph connectivity calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A network subgraph quality calculation in which an input data set describing internal nodes, edges and node degrees is used to determine the average node degree within the subgraph."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "intra subgraph connectivity calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200137.
obi:0200146 iao:0000111 "subgraph modularity calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A network subgraph quality calculation in which an input data set of subgraph in-degree and out-degree qualities is used to calculate the ratio of indegree to outdegree as a measure of modularity."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "subgraph modularity calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200137.
obi:0200147 iao:0000111 "network graph quality calculation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A network analysis in which an input data set describing node objects and edge relationships between node objects is used to determine the output quality of the network as a whole."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "network graph quality calculation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200080.
obi:0200149 iao:0000111 "unit-variance scaling"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A unit-variance scaling is a data transformation that divides all measurements of a variable by the standard deviation of that variable."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi"@en,
                        "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en;
            iao:0000118 "autoscaling"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PMID:16762068"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "unit-variance scaling"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200169.
obi:0200150 iao:0000111 "MA transformation";
            iao:0000112 "MA transformations are typically used in microarray data analyses. In this context, the g_i and r_i represent the reporter intensities in the two channels of a 2-channel assay or the reporter intensities in two related one-channel assays. Typically the base used for the logarithm is 2.";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "An MA transformation is a data transformation which takes as input a collection of data points (g_1, r_1), (g_2, r_2), ..., (g_n, r_n)  with the r_i and g_i positive real numbers, and whose output is the collection of data points (A_1, M_1), (A_2, M_2), ..., (A_n, M_n) where, for each i, A_i=(log(g_i)+log(r_i))/2 and M_i=log(r_i)-log(g_i). Here log denotes a logarithmic transformation.";
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi",
                        "Philippe Rocca-Serra";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "MA transformation";
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000.
obi:0200151 iao:0000111 "exponential base";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The exponential base is a feature of an exponential function which is defined in http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exponential_function. Its value can be any positive real number (typically different from 1).";
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi";
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exponential_function";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "exponential base"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom xsd:float ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000292 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200140.
obi:0200152 iao:0000111 "polynomial degree";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The polynomial degree is a feature of a polynomial function defined as the highest power of the polynomial's terms, where the terms of a polynomial are the individual summands with the coefficients omitted.";
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "polynomial degree"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000292 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200140.
obi:0200153 iao:0000111 "number of variables";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "The number of variables is a feature of any function (including polynomial functions) with domain contained in an n-dimensional vector space and is defined as n, the dimension of such space.";
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "number of variables"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom xsd:integer ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000292 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200140.
obi:0200154 iao:0000111 "agglomerative hierarchical clustering"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "An agglomerative hierarchical clustering is a hierarchical clustering which starts with separate clusters and then successively combines these clusters until there is only one cluster remaining."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi",
                        "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000118 "bottom-up hierarchical clustering";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "agglomerative hierarchical clustering"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200042.
obi:0200155 iao:0000111 "divisive hierarchical clustering"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A divisive hierarchical clustering is a hierarchical clustering which starts with a single cluster and then successively splits resulting clusters until only clusters of individual objects remain."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Elisabetta Manduchi",
                        "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000118 "top-down hierarchical clustering";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "divisive hierarchical clustering"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200042.
obi:0200156 iao:0000111 "data partitioning"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "Data partitioning is a data transformation with the objective of partitioning or separating input data into output subsets."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Ryan Brinkman"@en,
                        "PERSON: Richard Scheuermann"@en,
                        "PERSON: Melanie Courtot"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "data partitioning"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000.
obi:0200157 iao:0000111 "data vector reduction objective"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "Data vector reduction is a data transformation objective in which k m-dimensional input vectors are reduced to j m-dimensional output vectors, where j is smaller than k."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Richard H. Scheuermann"@en,
                        "James Malone";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Richard H. Scheuermann"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "data vector reduction objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200160 iao:0000111 "generalized family wise error rate correction method"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A generalized FWER correction method is a multiple testing procedure that controls the probability of at least k+1 false positives, where k is a user-supplied integer.";
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee";
            iao:0000118 "gFWER correction"@en;
            iao:0000119 "Dudoit, Sandrine and van der Laan, Mark J. (2008) Multiple Testing Procedures with Applications to Genomics.  New York: Springer , p. 19";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "generalized family wise error rate correction method"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200089,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000791 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200161 iao:0000111 "quantile number of false positives correction method"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A quantile number of false positives correction method is a MTP that controls for the pth quantile of the distribution of the number of false positives out of the total number of tests performed'";
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee";
            iao:0000118 "QNFP"@en;
            iao:0000119 "Dudoit, Sandrine and van der Laan, Mark J. (2008) Multiple Testing Procedures with Applications to Genomics.  New York: Springer , p. 19";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "quantile number of false positives correction method"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200089,
                            [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000662 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000791 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class].
obi:0200162 iao:0000111 "tail probability for the proportion of false positives correction method"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A TPPFP correction method is a MTP that controls the probability that the proportion of false positives among all rejected hypotheses is no greater than a constant q, where q is between 0 and 1.";
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee";
            iao:0000118 "TPPFP correction method"@en;
            iao:0000119 "Dudoit, Sandrine and van der Laan, Mark J. (2008) Multiple Testing Procedures with Applications to Genomics.  New York: Springer , p. 20";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "tail probability for the proportion of false positives correction method"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200089,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000791 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200163 iao:0000111 "false discovery rate correction method"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "The false discovery rate is a  data transformation used in multiple hypothesis testing to correct for multiple comparisons. It controls the expected proportion of incorrectly rejected null hypotheses (type I errors) in a list of rejected hypotheses. It is a less conservative comparison procedure with greater power than familywise error rate (FWER) control, at a cost of increasing the likelihood of obtaining type I errors. .";
            iao:0000116 """2011-03-31: [PRS]. 
creating a defined class by specifying the necessary output of dt
allows correct classification of FDR dt"""@en;
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en,
                        "Monnie McGee";
            iao:0000118 "FDR correction method"@en;
            iao:0000119 "Dudoit, Sandrine and van der Laan, Mark J. (2008) Multiple Testing Procedures with Applications to Genomics.  New York: Springer , p. 21 and http://www.wikidoc.org/index.php/False_discovery_rate";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "false discovery rate correction method"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200089,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000791 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000175 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction];
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0001442 ; 
                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                 a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200164 iao:0000111 "proportion of expected false positives correction method"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A proportion of expected false positives correction method is a multiple testing procedure that controls the ratio of the expected value of the numbers of false positives to the expected value of the numbers of rejected hypotheses.";
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee";
            iao:0000118 "PEFP correction method"@en;
            iao:0000119 "Dudoit, Sandrine and van der Laan, Mark J. (2008) Multiple Testing Procedures with Applications to Genomics.  New York: Springer , p. 21";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "proportion of expected false positives correction method"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200089,
                            [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000662 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000791 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class].
obi:0200165 iao:0000111 "quantile proportion of false positives correction method"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A quantile proportion of false positives correction method is a multiple testing procedure that controls the pth quantile of the distribution of the proportion of false positives among the rejected hypothesis (false discovery rate).";
            iao:0000117 "Monnie McGee";
            iao:0000118 "QPFP correction method"@en;
            iao:0000119 "Dudoit, Sandrine and van der Laan, Mark J. (2008) Multiple Testing Procedures with Applications to Genomics.  New York: Springer , p. 21";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "quantile proportion of false positives correction method"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200089,
                            [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000662 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]
                                                 [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000791 ; 
                                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class].
obi:0200166 iao:0000111 "data transformation objective"@en;
            iao:0000112 "normalize objective"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An objective specification to transformation input data into output data"@en;
            iao:0000116 "Modified definition in 2013 Philly OBI workshop";
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "data transformation objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000005.
obi:0200167 iao:0000111 "data normalization objective"@en;
            iao:0000112 """Quantile transformation which has normalization objective can be used for expression microarray assay normalization and it is referred to as \"quantile normalization\", according to the procedure described e.g. in PMID 12538238."""@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 """A normalization objective is a data transformation objective where the aim is to remove
systematic sources of variation to put the data on equal footing in order
to create a common base for comparisons."""@en;
            iao:0000117 "Helen Parkinson",
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi",
                        "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Helen Parkinson",
                        "PERSON: James Malone"@en,
                        "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "data normalization objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200168 iao:0000111 "correction objective"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Type I error correction"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A correction objective is a data transformation objective where the aim is to correct for error, noise or other impairments to the input of the data transformation or derived from the data transformation itself"@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone",
                        "PERSON: Melanie Courtot";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "correction objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200169 iao:0000111 "normalization data transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A normalization data transformation is a data transformation that has objective normalization."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "normalization data transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:unionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000451 ; 
                                              owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                              a owl:Restriction]
                                              [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200167 ; 
                                              owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                              a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                 a owl:Class].
obi:0200170 iao:0000111 "averaging data transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "An averaging data transformation is a data transformation that has objective averaging."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "averaging data transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:unionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000679 ; 
                                              owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                              a owl:Restriction]
                                              [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000425 ; 
                                              owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                              a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                 a owl:Class].
obi:0200171 iao:0000111 "partitioning data transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A partitioning data transformation is a data transformation that has objective partitioning."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "partitioning data transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200172 ; 
                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                 a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200172 iao:0000111 "partitioning objective"@en;
            iao:0000112 "A k-means clustering which has partitioning objective is a data transformation in which the input data is partitioned into k output sets."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A partitioning objective is a data transformation objective where the aim is to generate a collection of disjoint non-empty subsets whose union equals a non-empty input set."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "partitioning objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200173 iao:0000111 "background correction objective"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A background correction objective is a data transformation objective where the aim is to remove irrelevant contributions from the measured signal, e.g. those due to instrument noise or sample preparation."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "background correction objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200168.
obi:0200174 iao:0000111 "curve fitting objective"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A curve fitting objective is a data transformation objective in which the aim is to find a curve which matches a series of data points and possibly other constraints."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en,
                        "Elisabetta Manduchi";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "curve fitting objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200175 iao:0000111 "class discovery data transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A class discovery data transformation (sometimes called unsupervised classification) is a data transformation that has objective class discovery."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone";
            iao:0000118 "unsupervised classification data transformation",
                        "clustering data transformation";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "class discovery data transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:unionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000648 ; 
                                              owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                              a owl:Restriction]
                                              [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200178 ; 
                                              owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                              a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                 a owl:Class].
obi:0200176 iao:0000111 "Fisher's exact test";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "Fisher's exact test is a data transformation used to determine if there are nonrandom associations between two Fisher's exact test is a statistical significance test used in the analysis of contingency tables where sample sizes are small where the significance of the deviation from a null hypothesis can be calculated exactly, rather than relying on an approximation that becomes exact in the limit as the sample size grows to infinity, as with many statistical tests.";
            iao:0000117 "James Malone";
            iao:0000119 "WEB:http://mathworld.wolfram.com/FishersExactTest.html";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Fisher's exact test";
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000675 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000673.
obi:0200177 iao:0000111 "center calculation objective"@en;
            iao:0000112 "A mean calculation which has center calculation objective is a data transformation in which the center of the input data is discovered through the calculation of a mean average."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A center calculation objective is a data transformation objective where the aim is to calculate the center of an input data set."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "center calculation objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200178 iao:0000111 "class discovery objective"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A class discovery objective (sometimes called unsupervised classification) is a data transformation objective where the aim is to organize input data  (typically vectors of attributes) into classes, where the number of classes and their specifications are not known a priori. Depending on usage, the class assignment can be definite or probabilistic."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000118 "discriminant analysis objective"@en,
                        "clustering objective",
                        "unsupervised classification objective"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone",
                        "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "class discovery objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200179 iao:0000111 "class prediction objective"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 """A class prediction objective (sometimes called supervised classification) is a data transformation objective where the aim is to create a predictor from training data through a machine learning technique. The training data consist of pairs of objects (typically vectors of attributes) and
class labels for these objects. The resulting predictor can be used to attach class labels to any valid novel input object. Depending on usage, the prediction can be definite or probabilistic. A classification is learned from the training data and can then be tested on test data."""@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000118 "classification objective",
                        "supervised classification objective"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Elisabetta Manduchi",
                        "PERSON: James Malone";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "class prediction objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200180 iao:0000111 "spread calculation objective"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Spread calculation can be achieved by use of a standard deviation, which measures distance from the mean";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "is a data transformation objective whereby the aim is to the calculate the spread of a dataset, spread is a descriptive statistic which describes the variability of values in a data set ";
            iao:0000116 "Awaiting English definition from Monnie McGee"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Person:Helen Parkinson",
                        "James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "spread calculation objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200181 iao:0000111 "center calculation data transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A center calculation data transformation is a data transformation that has objective of center calculation."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "center calculation data transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:unionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000674 ; 
                                              owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                              a owl:Restriction]
                                              [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200177 ; 
                                              owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                              a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                 a owl:Class].
obi:0200182 iao:0000111 "data vector reduction data transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A data vector reduction is a data transformation that has objective data vector reduction and that consists of reducing the input vectors k to a smaller number of output vectors j, where j<k."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "data vector reduction data transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000707;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:unionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000676 ; 
                                              owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                              a owl:Restriction]
                                              [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200157 ; 
                                              owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                              a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                 a owl:Class].
obi:0200183 iao:0000111 "scaling objective"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Scaling gene expression data for cross platform analysis http://www.springerprotocols.com/Abstract/doi/10.1007/978-1-59745-454-4_13";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "is a data transformation objective where all, or some of a data set is adjusted by some data transformation according to some scale, for example a user defined minimum or maximum";
            iao:0000116 "Awaiting English definition from Monnie McGee"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Person:Helen Parkinson",
                        "James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "scaling objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200184 iao:0000111 "descriptive statistical calculation data transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A descriptive statistical calculation data transformation is a data transformation that has objective descriptive statistical calculation and which concerns any calculation intended to describe a feature of a data set, for example, its center or its variability."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "descriptive statistical calculation data transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:unionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000649 ; 
                                              owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                                              a owl:Restriction]
                                              [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200078 ; 
                                              owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                              a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                 a owl:Class].
obi:0200185 iao:0000111 "scaling data transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A scaling data transformation is a data transformation that has objective scaling."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "scaling data transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200183 ; 
                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                 a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200186 iao:0000111 "error correction objective"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Application of a multiple testing correction method";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "An error correction objective is a data transformation objective where the aim is to remove (correct for) erroneous contributions arising from the input data, or the transformation itself."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone, Helen Parkinson"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "error correction objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200168.
obi:0200187 iao:0000111 "sequence analysis data transformation"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A sequence analysis data transformation is a data transformation that has objective sequence analysis and has the aim of analysing ordered biological data for sequential patterns."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000119 "EDITOR";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "sequence analysis data transformation"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200081 ; 
                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                 a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200188 iao:0000111 "cross validation objective"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A cross validation objective is a data transformation objective in which the aim is to partition a sample of data into subsets such that the analysis is initially performed on a single subset, while the other subset(s) are retained for subsequent use in confirming and validating the initial analysis."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000118 "rotation estimation objective"@en;
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross_validation";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "cross validation objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200172.
obi:0200189 iao:0000111 "merging objective";
            iao:0000112 "merging of columns from two different data sets"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A merging objective is a data transformation objective in which the data transformation has the aim of performing a union of two or more sets."@en;
            iao:0000117 "James Malone"@en;
            iao:0000118 "combining objective"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Data Transformation Branch";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "merging objective"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200190 iao:0000111 "clustered data visualization";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A data visualization which has input of a clustered data set and produces an output of a report graph which is capable of rendering data of this type.";
            iao:0000117 "James Malone";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "clustered data visualization";
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:allValuesFrom obi:0000648 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom [owl:unionOf (iao:0000037
                                                              iao:0000179
                                                              iao:0000180
                                                              iao:0000183
                                                              iao:0000184) ; 
                                                 a owl:Class] ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200111.
obi:0200191 iao:0000111 "gene list visualization";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "Adata visualization which has input of a gene list and produces an output of a report graph which is capable of rendering data of this type.";
            iao:0000117 "James Malone";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "gene list visualization";
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:allValuesFrom obi:0000118 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom iao:0000306 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200111.
obi:0200192 iao:0000111 "classified data visualization";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A data visualization which has input of a classified data set and produces an output of a report graph which is capable of rendering data of this type.";
            iao:0000117 "James Malone";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "classified data visualization";
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:allValuesFrom obi:0000023 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom [owl:unionOf (iao:0000180
                                                              iao:0000184) ; 
                                                 a owl:Class] ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200111.
obi:0200193 iao:0000111 "background corrected data visualization";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A data visualization which has input of a background corrected data set and produces an output of a report graph which is capable of rendering data of this type.";
            iao:0000117 "James Malone",
                        "Monnie McGee";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "background corrected data visualization";
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom [owl:unionOf (iao:0000079
                                                              iao:0000179) ; 
                                                 a owl:Class] ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000299 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200111,
                            [owl:allValuesFrom obi:0000660 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200194 iao:0000111 "survival analysis data transformation";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A data transformation which has the objective of performing survival analysis.";
            iao:0000117 "James Malone";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: James Malone";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "survival analysis data transformation";
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200083 ; 
                                 owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                                 a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200195 iao:0000111 "proportional hazards model estimation";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "Proportional hazards model is a data transformation model to estimate the effects of different covariates influencing the times-to-failure of a system.";
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: James Malone",
                        "PERSON: Tina Boussard";
            iao:0000118 "Cox model",
                        "Cox proportional hazards model";
            iao:0000119 "WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cox_proportional_hazards_model";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "proportional hazards model estimation";
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200194,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200083 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200196 iao:0000111 "correlation study objective";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A data transformation objective in which correlation is obtained (often measured as a correlation coefficient, ρ) which indicates the strength and direction of a relationship between two random variables.";
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Tina Boussard";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "correlation study objective";
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200197 iao:0000111 "spectrum analysis objective";
            iao:0000112 "Calculation of characteristic path length in mass spectrometry";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "is a data transformation objective where the aim is to analyse some aspect of spectral data by some data transformation process. ";
            iao:0000117 "Person:Helen Parkinson",
                        "PERSON: Tina Boussard";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "spectrum analysis objective";
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200166.
obi:0200198 iao:0000111 "tandem mass spectrometry";
            iao:0000112 "A precursor ion is selected in the first stage, allowed to fragment and then all resultant masses are scanned in the second mass analyzer and detected in the detector that is positioned after the second mass analyzer. This experiment is commonly performed to identify transitions used for quantification by tandem MS.";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "Tandem mass spectrometry is a data transformation that uses two or more analyzers separated by a region in which ions can be induced to fragment by transfer of energy (frequently by collision with other molecules).";
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: James Malone",
                        "PERSON: Tina Boussard";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Tina Boussard";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "tandem mass spectrometry";
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200085,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200197 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0200199 iao:0000111 "gas chromatography mass spectrometry";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 """Gas chromatography mass spectrometry is a data transformation combining mass spectrometry and  
gas chromatography for the qualitative as well as quantitative  
determinations of compounds.""";
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: James Malone",
                        "PERSON: Tina Boussard";
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Tina Boussard";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "gas chromatography mass spectrometry";
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0200197 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0200085.
obi:0200200 iao:0000111 "chi square test";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "The chi-square test is a data transformation with the objective of statistical hypothesis testing, in which the sampling distribution of the test statistic is a chi-square distribution when the null hypothesis is true, or any in which this is asymptotically true, meaning that the sampling distribution (if the null hypothesis is true) can be made to approximate a chi-square distribution as closely as desired by making the sample size large enough.";
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Tina Boussard",
                        "PERSON: James Malone";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "chi square test";
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000675 ; 
                             owl:onProperty obi:0000417 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000673.
obi:0200201 iao:0000111 "ANOVA";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "ANOVA or analysis of variance is a data transformation in which a statistical test of whether the means of several groups are all equal.";
            iao:0000117 "James Malone";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "ANOVA";
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0200000.
obi:0300310 iao:0000111 "sequential design"@en;
            iao:0000112 "PMID: 17710740.Pharm Stat. 2007 Aug 20.Sequential design approaches for bioequivalence studies with crossover designs."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "Any design in which the decision as to whether to enroll the next patient, pair of patients, or block of patients is determined by whether the cumulative treatment difference for all previous patients is within specified limits.  Enrollment is continued if the difference does not exceed the limits.  It is terminated if it does"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en;
            iao:0000119 "MUSC"@en;
            iao:0000232 "Provenance: OCI"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "sequential design"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000115.
obi:0300311 iao:0000111 "observation design"@en;
            iao:0000112 "PMID: 12387964.Lancet. 2002 Oct 12;360(9340):1144-9.Deficiency of antibacterial peptides in patients with morbus Kostmann: an observation study."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "observation design is a study design in which subjects are monitored in the absence of any active intervention by experimentalists."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OBI branch derived"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "observation design"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0500000.
obi:0302714 iao:0000111 "collection (of entities of organismal origin)"@en;
            iao:0000112 "PMID: 18037794. Magn Reson Med Sci. 2007;6(3):139-46. Imaging of a large collection of human embryo using a super-parallel MR microscope.[the Orsay Museum has a nice collection of Impressionnist paintings]"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "a collection is a bfo:aggregate object, that is a set of material object of the same kind"@en;
            iao:0000116 "2009-11-04, MC: Entity of organismal origin has been deprecated a while ago. We still have collection (of entities of organismal origin). I am not sure we could replace with collection of material entity without altering the meaning (i.e. deprecating the class). In addition, if we do deprecate that class, should we just assert the children under material entity?",
                        "03/17/2010: obsoleted (on call), and replaced by 'material entity' and/or specimen. No need for the 'collection' part of this class any more after merging bfo:aggregate object into material entity, and by dealing with 'specimen' rather than with entities of organismal origin.",
                        "added during 22-02-2008 biomaterial call to distinguish library and population"@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Susanna Sansone";
            iao:0000118 "set, group, ensemble"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en;
            iao:0000231 iao:0000103;
            iao:0000232 "PRS: How can we distinguish with 'collection' as the process of collecting entities, (eg. data collection, urine collection)"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "obsolete_collection (of entities of organismal origin)"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf oboinowl:ObsoleteClass;
            owl:deprecated true.
obi:0302716 iao:0000111 "pool of specimens"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A pool of specimens is a mixture of a population of samples which have been gathered from one or more sample populations, obtained by the physical process of mixing individual specimens, e.g.  mixing the DNA collected from the individual fish."@en;
            iao:0000116 "check with advisors as to how to represent multiple instances of any class? a set of specimens which have been gathered from one or more sample_populations, obtained by the physical process of mixing individual specimens, e.g.  mixing the DNA collected from the individual fish"@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Jennifer Fostel";
            iao:0000119 "GROUP: CEBS";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "pool of specimens"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000953;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:intersectionOf (obi:0100051
                                                     [owl:someValuesFrom [owl:intersectionOf (obi:0000652
                                                                                             [owl:allValuesFrom obi:0100051 ; 
                                                                                             owl:onProperty obi:0000293 ; 
                                                                                             a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                                                         a owl:Class] ; 
                                                     owl:onProperty obi:0000312 ; 
                                                     a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                 a owl:Class].
obi:0302729 iao:0000111 "chemical solution"@en;
            iao:0000112 "PMID: 18289311.Anesth Analg. 2008 Apr;106(4):1078-86.Less impairment of hemostasis and reduced blood loss in pigs after resuscitation from hemorrhagic shock using the small-volume concept with hypertonic saline/hydroxyethyl starch as compared to administration of 4% gelatin or 6% hydroxyethyl starch solution."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A material entity  that is made up of at least 2 scattered molecular aggregates, one playing the role of solvent and the other one playing the role of solute."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Philippe Rocca-Serra",
                        "PERSON: Bjoern Peters";
            iao:0000118 "liquid chemical solution"@en;
            iao:0000119 "GROUP: OBI Biomaterial Branch";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "chemical solution"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000040;
            owl:equivalentClass [owl:intersectionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom [owl:intersectionOf (obi:0000576
                                                                                             [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0302732 ; 
                                                                                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000087 ; 
                                                                                             a owl:Restriction]) ; 
