            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "cell lysis is a process by which cell membrane integrity of live cells  is compromised and leads to cell death. Cell lysis may be achieved by means of viral action or osmotic shock."@en;
            iao:0000116 "BP, JG, RV: There is also a need for the unplanned cell lysis, which is probably not in the scope of OBI, but should be linked to from this process.";
