obi:0400120 iao:0000111 "temperature control bath"@en;
            iao:0000112 "VWR Signature Deep-Chamber Heated Water Bath. A water bath is used for temperatures up to 100 degrees C. An oil bath is employed for temperatures over 100 degrees C."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A temperature_control_bath is a device that has the function to regulate the temperature of a material, the function to contain fluid and the function to vary and maintain the temperature of the contained fluid. Heat exchange (energy transfer) between the material and the heating element is facilitated via the contained fluid. A temperature_control_bath is composed of a container, a heating element and/or a cooling element and a means to adjust the needed temperature. In most cases also a timer and a means to stir the fluid is provided as well."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson",
                        "Alan Ruttenburg",
                        "Daniel Schober";
            iao:0000119 "OBI Instrument branch";
            iao:0000232 "DS: This was heated_bath. It was renamed to reflect the possability that the same bath can be used for cooling. We can now define the temperature variables and based on that infer if it is a cooling device or a heating device (also quite relative to surrounding temperature)."@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "temperature control bath"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000370 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000401 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0002089.
obi:0400121 iao:0000111 "molecular crosslinker"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Stratalinker"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "a device that is able to chemically join two or more molecules."@en;
            iao:0000116 """AL: if we intend that other ontologies can be used in conjunction with OBI, we shouldn't have such a general term used specifically for chemically joining two or more molecules. I'm sure there are other \"crosslinkers\" that are on a much different scale in engineering etc. I have moved the original label to be an alternative term, and have renamed the main label accordingly."""@en;
            iao:0000117 "Trish Whetzel"@en;
            iao:0000118 "molecular crosslinker"@en;
            iao:0000119 "MO ?? cannot be found in MO"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "molecular crosslinker"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0001032,
                            obi:0002089,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000367 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000401 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0400135 iao:0000111 "image cytometer"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The most common current application of image cytometry is for DNA analysis, followed by quantitation of immunohistochemical staining."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "An image_cytometer is an instrument for image-based study or measurement of cells."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Melanie Courtot"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://web.mit.edu/solab/Research/ImageCytometry.html"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "image cytometer"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0400082 ; 
