                                                 owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000051 ; 
                                                 a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                             a owl:Class],
                            obi:0000832.
obi:0400140 iao:0000111 "gel tank"@en;
            iao:0000112 "CHEF gel box, slab gel box, capillary electrophoresis"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "a device which holds a gel and running buffers to allow electrophoresis to be performed. A gel tank has the function to contain and to control the contained environment and transfer energy from an energy supply through the running buffers to the gel matrix and the material with charged molecules in an electric field across a porous matrix or medium with the objective to separate the charged molecules."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Person:Kevin Clancy"@en,
                        "Person:Frank Gibson";
            iao:0000118 "electrophoresis box"@en,
                        "electrophoresis unit"@en;
            iao:0000119 "sep:00095"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "gel tank"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000370 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0002089,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000401 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0400142 iao:0000111 "power supply"@en;
            iao:0000112 "A AC/DC transformer that generates the reqired power for an electrophoresis apparatus"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000125;
            iao:0000115 "A power supply is an device or part of a device that permits the required application of a defined electrical charge to an instrument. The power supply may permit the defined application of a given amount of current for a defined length of time."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Frank Gibson",
                        "Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000118 "power pack"@en,
                        "PSU"@en,
                        "power supply unit"@en,
                        "electrical power supply"@en;
            iao:0000119 "sep:00093",
                        "PERSON: Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000232 "was power_pack, maps to SEP electrical_power_supply"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "power supply"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000384 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000968.
obi:0400143 iao:0000111 "fluorometer"@en;
            iao:0000112 "laser/detector in capillary electrophoresis apparatus, NanoDrop ND-3300"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A fluorometer is an instrument for the detection and measurement of parameters of fluoresence, which in turn are used to identify the presence and amount of specific molecules in the sample."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Kevin Lister"@en,
                        "Allyson Lister"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OBI"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "fluorometer"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0400115.
obi:0400146 iao:0000111 "multispectral imaging flow cytometer"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A multispectral_imaging_flow_cytometer is an instrument which combines quantitative image analysis and flow cytometry in a single platform. It measures the amount, location and movement of molecules on, in, or between cells, and  the location and co-localization of multiple markers on or in cells. It can also quantitate morphologically distinct cell subpopulations."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Melanie Courtot"@en;
            iao:0000118 "MIFC"@en;
            iao:0000119 "http://www.amnis.com/"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "multispectral imaging flow cytometer"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000392 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            obi:0000398,
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0400044 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:BFO_0000051 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction],
                            [owl:someValuesFrom obi:0000397 ; 
                             owl:onProperty pobo:RO_0000085 ; 
                             a owl:Restriction].
obi:0400147 iao:0000111 "microarray"@en;
            iao:0000112 "An affymetrix U133 array is a microarray. Microarrays include 1 and 2-color arrays, custom and commercial arrays (e.g, Affymetrix, Agilent, Nimblegen, Illumina, etc.) for expression profiling, DNA variant detection, protein binding, and other genomic and functional genomic assays.";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A processed material that is made to be used in an analyte assay. It consists of a physical immobilisation matrix in which substances that bind the analyte are placed in regular spatial position."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Chris Stoeckert";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "microarray"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0001865.
obi:0400148 iao:0000111 "DNA microarray"@en;
            iao:0000112 """Moran G, Stokes C, Thewes S, Hube B, Coleman DC, Sullivan D (2004). \"Comparative genomics using Candida albicans DNA microarrays reveals absence and divergence of virulence-associated genes in Candida dubliniensis\". Microbiology 150: 3363-3382. doi:10.1099/mic.0.27221-0. PMID 15470115"""@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "A DNA-microarray is a microarray that is used as a physical 2D immobilisation matrix for DNA sequences. DNA microarray-bound DNA fragments are used as targets for a hybridising probed sample."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Frank Gibson",
                        "PERSON: Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000118 "DNA Chip"@en,
                        "DNA-array"@en;
            iao:0000119 "Web:<http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DNA_microarray>@2008/03/03";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "DNA microarray"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0400147.
obi:0400149 iao:0000111 "protein microarray"@en;
            iao:0000112 "The most common protein microarray is the antibody microarray, where antibodies are spotted onto the protein chip and are used as capture molecules to detect proteins from cell lysate solutions."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A protein-microarray is a microarray, ususlly a piece of glass, on which different molecules of protein have been affixed at separate locations in an ordered manner. These are used to identify protein-protein or protein-small molecule interactions."@en;
            iao:0000117 "Daniel Schober"@en;
            iao:0000119 "PERSON: Daniel Schober";
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "protein microarray"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf obi:0400147.
obi:0400153 iao:0000111 "droplet sorter"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 """A droplet sorter is part_of a flow cytometer sorter that converts the carrier fluid stream into individual droplets, and these droplets are directed into separate locations for recovery (enriching the original
sample for particles of interest based on qualities determined by gating) or disposal."""@en;
            iao:0000117 "OBI Instrument branch";
