            iao:0000114 iao:0000123;
            iao:0000115 "is the process in which an adaptive immune receptor binds to a material entity (realizing its disposition). The binding affinity is significant enough to trigger an immune response. Specifically, transient non-specific binding of adaptive immune receptors occurring during immune surveillance is not considered significant binding."@en;
