vo:0000001 iao:0000111 "vaccine";
           iao:0000115 "A vaccine is a processed material with the function that when administered, it prevents or ameliorates a disorder in a target organism by inducing or modifying adaptive immune responses specific to the antigens in the vaccine.";
           iao:0000412 pobo:vo.owl;
           a owl:Class;
           rdfs:label "vaccine";
           rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000040.
vo:0000002 iao:0000111 "vaccination";
           iao:0000115 "a process of administering substance in vivo that involves in adding a vaccine into a host (e.g., human) in vivo with the intent to invoke a protective or therapeutic adaptive immune response.";
